#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:165
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:180
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:196
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:212
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:228
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:244
msgid "Orcs"
msgstr "オーク"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:151
msgid ""
"They headed northwest, deeper into the forest, to evade orcish patrols and "
"buy themselves a moment of respite."
msgstr ""
"Wesnoth と エルフの連合隊は北西を目指していました。オークの巡回警備から逃れ束"
"の間の休息を得るため、森の奥深くへと入っていきました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:154
msgid ""
"For that, however, they would need to gather supplies and find a safe place "
"to hide."
msgstr "そのためには、食料などを調達し、安全な避難場所を探す必要がありました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:157
msgid ""
"Chapter Fourteen\n"
"<i>Laying Low</i>"
msgstr ""
"第14章\n"
"<i>隠伏 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:190
msgid ""
"There are multiple large caves near us that we could use to hide for some "
"time."
msgstr ""
"この近くに大きな洞窟がたくさんあるから、暫くはそこに隠れていられるわね。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:194
msgid ""
"We'll need food at the very least for a few days... and we'll need to make "
"sure the cave is safe."
msgstr ""
"少なくとも数日分の食料が必要でしょう...それと、洞窟が安全かどうかも確かめねば"
"なりません。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:198
msgid "We also need to do it fast, before orcish patrols come around."
msgstr "それに、オークの巡回警備が来る前に、迅速に行う必要がありますわ。"

#. [message]: speaker=second_unit
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:217
msgid "Wolves!"
msgstr "あっ、狼がいる！"

#. [message]: id=CF, ES, EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:226
msgid "Yeah... Let's try finding a better food source first..."
msgstr "ええ... もっと良い食料源を探してみましょう..."

#. [message]: speaker=second_unit
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:249
msgid "There are boars here!"
msgstr "ここにはイノシシが！"

#. [message]: id=CF, ES, EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:258
msgid ""
"That could be enough edible food, at least until we're sure no patrols will "
"come around. Let's hunt them!"
msgstr ""
"少なくとも、周辺にオークの警備が来ないと確信できるまでは、十分、食用になりそ"
"うですね。さあ、あの獲物を捕まえましょう！"

#. [message]: speaker=second_unit
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:271
msgid "There is a cave here. And a bear!"
msgstr "ここに洞窟があります。それと、......クマも！"

#. [message]: id=CF, ES, EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:280
msgid "That cave seems small, it won't be enough."
msgstr "その洞窟は小さそうですね、他を探しましょう。"

#. [message]: id=EA, ES, CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:289
msgid "We'll take out the bear and look elsewhere."
msgstr "クマは持ち帰って、他の洞窟を探しましょう。"

#. [message]: speaker=second_unit
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:302
msgid "That cave seems big enough. Wait, spider!"
msgstr "あの洞窟の大きさは十分そうです。待ってください、蜘蛛が！"

#. [message]: id=EA, ES, CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:311
msgid "Let us kill it and then we shall have shelter."
msgstr "蜘蛛をやっつけて、避難場所にしましょう。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:333
msgid "We should have more than enough now."
msgstr "食料はもうこれで十分でしょう。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:355
msgid "Good, then we need only find a cave to hole up in."
msgstr "良かった、それなら、あとは身を隠す洞窟を見つけるだけですね。"

#. [message]: speaker=second_unit
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:372
msgid "There is more than enough room in this cave!"
msgstr "この洞窟なら、十分すぎるほど広いですね！"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:397
msgid "Good, then we need only find food."
msgstr "良かった、それなら、あとは食料を探すだけですね。"

#. [message]: type=Goblin Knight
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:412
msgid "Ha, found 'em! Warn the chief."
msgstr "ガハハ、見つけたぞ！　首領に知らせろ。"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:417
msgid "No! They found us!"
msgstr "いけないわ！見つかってしまったわ！"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:429
msgid "Well, we've got roof and board. I believe that should do it."
msgstr "えーと、屋根と板がありますね。これで十分だと思います。"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:433
msgid "Indeed, let us hurry to cover our tracks."
msgstr "ですね。さあ、足跡などを消しましょうか、急ぎましょう。"

#. [message]: type=Goblin Knight
#: war_and_home/scenarios/14_Laying_Low.cfg:466
msgid "No trace of 'em here, let's move on."
msgstr "ここにはヤツラの痕跡はないな、他を探すぞ。"

#. [scenario]: id=15_A_Brief_Respite
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:5
msgid "A Brief Respite"
msgstr "束の間の休息"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:148
msgid ""
"Though orcish forces came quite close, the humans and elves proved too "
"elusive for them."
msgstr ""
"オーク軍はすぐ近くまで追ってきていたのですが、人間とエルフの連合軍は非常に捕"
"まえにくいことが分かりました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:151
msgid ""
"Now, all that remained was to heal the wounded and wait.\n"
"\n"
"Wait until the enemy left the surroundings and to try and make the best out "
"of this moment of calm."
msgstr ""
"さあ、残るは、負傷者の傷を手当して待つだけでした。\n"
"\n"
"周囲の敵がいなくなるまで待って、静寂の瞬間を最大限に利用するのです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:156
msgid ""
"Chapter Fifteen\n"
"<i>A Brief Respite</i>"
msgstr ""
"第14章\n"
"<i>束の間の休息 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:181
msgid "Are we good on rations and medical supplies?"
msgstr "食料と医療品は大丈夫かい？"

#. [message]: type=Longbowman
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:185
msgid ""
"Yes sir, we have enough of everything for now if we keep with the current "
"rationing."
msgstr "はい、士官殿、現在の食料配給量であれば、不足はありません。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:189
msgid "Good, in that case keep the setup going."
msgstr "よっしゃ、それなら作業を続けるように。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:200
msgid "How are the wounded?"
msgstr "負傷者の様子はどうです？"

#. [message]: type=Elvish Druid
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:204
msgid "All of them are stable and improving gradually."
msgstr "全員が安定していて、徐々に快方に向かっています。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:208
msgid "Great, please keep at it!"
msgstr "素晴らしい、今後もその調子でお願いしますよ！"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:219
msgid "(<i>To Anówien</i>) He is taking good care of the troops isn't he?"
msgstr "（<i>Anówien に向かって </i>）彼、軍隊の面倒見がいいわよね？"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:223
msgid "Indeed, and you have been observing him quite carefully, haven't you?"
msgstr "ほんとね。あなたも、彼のことを随分と入念に観察してるようだけど、違う？"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:227
msgid "What, n—no, I just started looking..."
msgstr "な、何よ、違うわよ。今、初めて見てみたところよ...."

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:231
msgid ""
"Oh my, I'm going to have fun! (<i>To Caror</i>) Caror, could you come here "
"please?"
msgstr ""
"あらぁ、楽しくなりそうねえ！（<i>Caror に向かって </i>）Caror 、ちょっと、こ"
"ちらに来てもらえないかしら？"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:235
msgid "Mother! What are you doing!"
msgstr "お母さま！何をしてるのよ！"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:252
msgid "Yes? What's the problem?"
msgstr "はい...ん？どうされました？"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:256
msgid ""
"We're going to be in forested areas for some time still, Sylindë can help "
"you handle it better."
msgstr ""
"もう暫くの間、森林地帯にいることになるでしょう。Sylindë があなたをうまくサ"
"ポートしてくれますよ。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:260
msgid "U—uh, th—thank you for the offer, I'd appreciate it."
msgstr "えーと、あ、有難うございます、ご提案いただいたことに感謝します。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/15_A_Brief_Respite.cfg:264
msgid "Y—yes, follow me, we'll do some training in the woods outside."
msgstr "あー...えぇ、こちらへどうぞ、外縁の森で訓練でもしましょう。"

#. [scenario]: id=16_To_The_Harbour
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:5
msgid "To The Harbour"
msgstr "港へ向かう"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:124
msgid ""
"After a few weeks, enemy presence lightened considerably, providing an "
"opportunity to move out."
msgstr "数週間後、敵の存在はかなり薄れてきて、移動を始める機会が訪れました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:127
msgid ""
"A simple plan was agreed upon. They would head to the nearest port and use "
"whatever boats were there. They would then head downriver, evading the main "
"enemy forces."
msgstr ""
"簡単な計画がまとまりました。一番近い港へ向かい、そこにある船を利用するので"
"す。そうして、敵の主力部隊を避けながら下流へと向かう、というものでした。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:130
msgid ""
"Chapter Sixteen\n"
"<i>To The Harbour</i>"
msgstr ""
"第17章\n"
"<i>港へ向かう </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:153
msgid "Finally, we have reached the harbour!"
msgstr "遂に、港に着きましたわね！"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:157
msgid "Indeed, and we arrived quite fast. It seems the training was useful."
msgstr "ええ、それに、かなり早く到着しましたね。訓練が役立ったようですね。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:161
msgid "Y—yes, it was extremely helpful..."
msgstr "あ、はい、大変、役に立ちました..."

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:165
msgid "I would hope so, seeing how much time you two spent together."
msgstr ""
"そうであってほしいですね、二人が一緒に過ごした時間が物語っているようです。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:169
msgid "M—Mother! A—Anyway, we should hurry and take them out."
msgstr "お、お母さま！ と、とにかく、急いでここから皆を連れ出さなきゃ。"

#. [message]: speaker=OL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:175
msgid "Enemies! To arms!"
msgstr "敵だぜ！武器を取れ！"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:179
msgid "Well then, kill'em all."
msgstr "よし、全員殺すんだ。"

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:234
msgid ""
"Caror now has more movement points, better defences and better movement "
"costs."
msgstr ""
"Caror は移動ポイントが 1 増え、攻撃回避率が向上し、移動コストが改善されまし"
"た。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:249
msgid "We're caught in a pincer!"
msgstr "挟み撃ちにされた！"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:259
msgid "Well that's done. Now for the rest."
msgstr "さあ、これで終わりですね。やっと休めるわ。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:263
msgid "We have enough boats here for everyone!"
msgstr "ここには十分な船がありますよ、皆さんのために！"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/16_To_The_Harbour.cfg:267
msgid "In that case, let us embark and head downriver."
msgstr "それでは、乗船して下流へと向かいましょう。"

#. [scenario]: id=17_Break_Through
#: war_and_home/scenarios/17_Break_Through.cfg:5
msgid "Break Through"
msgstr "突破"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/17_Break_Through.cfg:141
msgid ""
"Though they now had transportation, it still required a clear waterway to be "
"useful."
msgstr ""
"輸送する交通手段はできましたが、有効な水路が確保できること、それが必要でし"
"た。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/17_Break_Through.cfg:144
msgid ""
"And that, they lacked.\n"
"\n"
"In their way stood the River Gates, a fortified bridge who once controlled "
"naval entry into the kingdom, now fallen into the hands of orcs."
msgstr ""
"そして、それこそが、大きな問題だったのです。\n"
"\n"
"彼らの行く手には、水門 \"the River Gates\"が立ちはだかっていました。かつては"
"海軍が王国への進入を統制していた要塞橋ですが、今ではオークの手に落ちていまし"
"た。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/17_Break_Through.cfg:149
msgid "They would need to storm the fortress to escape the ruins of home."
msgstr "故郷の廃墟から脱出するためには、その要塞を襲撃する必要があったのです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/17_Break_Through.cfg:152
msgid ""
"Chapter Seventeen\n"
"<i>Break Through</i>"
msgstr ""
"第17章\n"
"<i>突破 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/17_Break_Through.cfg:174
msgid "Take out the guards on the bridge and we'll have a way out!"
msgstr "橋上の衛兵を倒せば、脱出できるはずです！"

#. [message]: speaker=OL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/17_Break_Through.cfg:178
msgid ""
"Humans and elves are attacking the forts! Hold them back until "
"reinforcements arrive!"
msgstr "人間とエルフが砦を攻撃してるぞ！援軍が着くまで、頑張って持ちこたえろ！"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/17_Break_Through.cfg:182
msgid "We need to take them out and fast!"
msgstr "さっさと敵を倒さなければ。急ぐのよ！"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/17_Break_Through.cfg:186
msgid "Agreed. Let's get to it."
msgstr "その通りですね、やりましょう。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/17_Break_Through.cfg:201
msgid "No! Their reinforcements are here, we'll be caught here!"
msgstr "駄目だわ！敵の援軍がやって来たわ、ここで捕えられてしまう！"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/17_Break_Through.cfg:210
msgid "The bridge is under our control now. The boats can cross."
msgstr "橋は、私たちの統制下となりました。船が通れます。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/17_Break_Through.cfg:214
msgid "Then let us reembark as fast as possible, before more enemies show up."
msgstr "さあ、できるだけ早く出航しましょう。敵がもっと現れる前に。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/17_Break_Through.cfg:218
msgid "Indeed, for the road left until Wesnoth is quite long."
msgstr "ええ、Wesnoth までには、まだまだ長い道のりが残されていますから。"

#. [scenario]: id=18_Fateful_Reunion
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:10
msgid "Fateful Reunion"
msgstr "運命的な再会"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:130
msgid ""
"It was smooth sailing afterwards, with a disembark around the confluence "
"with the Arkan-Thoria."
msgstr ""
"その後の船での旅程は文字通り順風満帆で、Arkan-Thoria と合流するあたりで下船し"
"ました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:133
msgid ""
"The journey on foot following it happened without incident. At least, until "
"they reached Merlyc."
msgstr ""
"その後、徒歩による旅程は、問題なく順調に進められました。少なくとも、 Merlyc "
"に到着するまでは。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:136
msgid ""
"Chapter Eighteen\n"
"<i>Fateful Reunion</i>"
msgstr ""
"第18章\n"
"<i>運命的な再会 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=BL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:217
msgid "This town is ours, leave us alone!"
msgstr "この町は俺たちのもんだ、さっさと失せろ！"

#. [message]: speaker=NB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:221
msgid "It is within the realm of Wesnoth and as such, under its protection!"
msgstr "ここは Wesnoth 領内だ、しかるに、その管理下にあるのだ！"

#. [message]: speaker=EN
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:225
msgid "You will terrorize its people no longer!"
msgstr "これ以上、民衆を恐怖に陥れるべきではない！"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:229
msgid ""
"(<i>To Caror</i>) I thought these lands were protected by Wesnoth's armies."
msgstr ""
"（<i>Caror に向かって </i>）この地は Wesnoth 軍の保護下にあると思っていたので"
"すが。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:233
msgid ""
"We defended Merlyc from a bandit raid before heading North. I fear it fell "
"later."
msgstr ""
"北へ向かう前に、私たちは盗賊たちの襲撃から Merlyc を守りましたが、後で陥落し"
"ないか心配です。"

#. [message]: speaker=BL2
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:237
msgid "More enemies from the North!"
msgstr "北側からもっと敵が来たぞ！"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:241
msgid "And now they saw us... Wait, Lumiclya?"
msgstr "今、彼らが私たちを見た... ちょっと待って、 Lumiclya じゃない？"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:245
msgid "Sylindë and Anówien! We thought you were all lost to us!"
msgstr "Sylindë と Anówien よ！みんなとは、もう会えないと思っていたわ！"

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:249
msgid "And Caror as well! You were having fun in the forest, weren't you..."
msgstr "それに Caror も！森の中で楽しくやっていたのですね..."

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:253
msgid "N—no... Anyway, we'll swap tales later. First, let's take them out."
msgstr ""
"え、いや、まさか... とにかく、後ほど、話を交わしましょう。先ずは、奴らを倒し"
"ましょう。"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:268
msgid "No! We had lost them!"
msgstr "駄目です、見失ってしまったのです！"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:277
msgid ""
"Finally, they are dealt with. Now, while we have some time, I believe some "
"stories are long overdue."
msgstr ""
"やっと決着がつきました。さて、時間ができましたが、じっくり話すことがあるかと"
"思います。"

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/18_Fateful_Reunion.cfg:281
msgid "Indeed, I believe there are."
msgstr "本当に。私もそう思います。"

#. [scenario]: id=19_Not_In_Vain
#: war_and_home/scenarios/19_Not_In_Vain.cfg:5
msgid "Not In Vain"
msgstr "無駄にはしない"

#. [objective]: condition=lose
#: war_and_home/scenarios/19_Not_In_Vain.cfg:26
msgid ""
"Any enemy unit reaches the docks (is closer to them than your own units)"
msgstr "敵ユニットが船着場に到着する（敵は自軍ユニットよりもドックに近い）"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/19_Not_In_Vain.cfg:261
msgid ""
"After the victory, tales were told and tears were shed. Both of sadness for "
"the lost and joy for the living."
msgstr ""
"勝利の後、それぞれの物語が語られ、涙が流されました。失った者への悲しみと、生"
"きている者への喜びの両方がありました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/19_Not_In_Vain.cfg:264
msgid ""
"They decided to evacuate over the Great River and within Wesnoth's "
"heartlands as Merlyc would not hold against a massive orcish assault."
msgstr ""
"Merlyc の街はオークの大規模な襲撃に持ちこたえられないので、王女たちは the "
"Great River を越えて Wesnoth の中核地域に避難することに決めたのでした。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/19_Not_In_Vain.cfg:267
msgid ""
"Though the retreat proceeded apace, there would be bloodshed ere its end."
msgstr "退却は速やかに進みましたが、その前には流血の惨禍もあったのです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/19_Not_In_Vain.cfg:270
msgid ""
"Chapter Nineteen\n"
"<i>Not In Vain</i>"
msgstr ""
"第19章\n"
"<i>無駄にはしない </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=BB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/19_Not_In_Vain.cfg:289
msgid "You have nowhere to run. Surrender and some of you might survive."
msgstr ""
"お前たちに逃げ場はないぞ。投降すれば、生き延びられる者もいるかもしれんがな。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/19_Not_In_Vain.cfg:293
msgid "We will not fall to you! Your forces will break against our walls!"
msgstr ""
"そんなことなど、するわけがない！そっちの軍は、この城壁相手に暴れているがい"
"い！"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/19_Not_In_Vain.cfg:297
msgid ""
"We will hold until the last ship departs! Leave no one behind, that those "
"who fell did so for a reason!"
msgstr ""
"最後の船が出帆するまで持ちこたえなさい！誰も置き去りにしてはいけない！倒れた"
"者にも理由はあるのですよ！"

#. [message]: speaker=B1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/19_Not_In_Vain.cfg:301
msgid "Looks like we've got a lot of people to kill! This'll be fun!"
msgstr "殺されたい奴が、た～くさんいるようだな！こりゃ楽しくなりそうだぜ！"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/19_Not_In_Vain.cfg:319
msgid "The last transport is here, embark and leave!"
msgstr "これが最後の輸送船です。乗り込んでください、出発します！"

#. [message]: speaker=EN
#: war_and_home/scenarios/19_Not_In_Vain.cfg:323
msgid "Finally, we're out!"
msgstr "遂に、脱出だ！"

#. [message]: speaker=BB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/19_Not_In_Vain.cfg:327
msgid "Nooo! Do not let them leave!"
msgstr "うぬぬぬぬ～！　逃がすな！"

#. [message]: speaker=BB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/19_Not_In_Vain.cfg:343
msgid "Impossible! Fall back!"
msgstr "くそ、駄目だ！　撤退するぞ!"

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/19_Not_In_Vain.cfg:388
msgid ""
"They have gotten between us and the docks, we won't be able to evacuate!"
msgstr "奴ら、我々と船着場の間に侵入してきたわ、避難するなんて無理よ！"

#. [scenario]: id=20_Arrival_And_Warning
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:5
msgid "Arrival And Warning"
msgstr "到着と警告"

#. [side]: id=HK, type=Royal Warrior
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:107
msgid "King Garard I of Wesnoth"
msgstr "Wesnoth 王, Garard Ⅰ世"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:148
msgid ""
"Once within Wesnoth, everyone separated into multiple groups to handle their "
"duties: to take care of the displaced civilians, to warn the king and to "
"rally support for the war."
msgstr ""
"かつて Wesnoth では、国民は皆、役目を果たすために複数のグループに分かれていま"
"した。役目とは、避難民の世話、国王への警告、戦争への支援取りまとめなどでし"
"た。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:151
msgid ""
"Chapter Twenty\n"
"<i>Arrival And Warning</i>"
msgstr ""
"第20章\n"
"<i>到着と警告 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=HG1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:181
msgid "Your Majesty, they have arrived."
msgstr "陛下、彼らが到着しました。"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:185
msgid "Your Highness, we are most honored by your welcome in our time of need."
msgstr "国王陛下、このような時にお迎えいただき、大変光栄に存じます。"

#. [message]: speaker=HK
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:189
msgid ""
"It is but our duty to assist our allies, think nothing of it. Please, relate "
"to me these dreadful events."
msgstr ""
"同盟国を支援するのは我々の義務だから、何も考えなくてよいのだよ。さあ、この恐"
"ろしい出来事を私に話してもらえるかな。"

#. [message]: speaker=HK
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:206
msgid ""
"This is truly despicable and the kingdom of Wesnoth shall respond with its "
"full might."
msgstr ""
"これは正に卑しむべき行為であり、Wesnoth 王国は、その全力をもって対処するもの"
"とする。"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:210
msgid "We thank you for your steadfast support."
msgstr "陛下の確固たるご支援に感謝いたします。"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:264
msgid "I fear I shall need to remain in Weldyn for some time, politicking."
msgstr ""
"私はしばらく Weldyn に留まって、政治的取引を行う必要があるだろうと心配してい"
"ます。"

#. [message]: speaker=NB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:268
msgid ""
"I will remain to try and assist with the court while my sister informs our "
"parents."
msgstr ""
"私は、妹が両親に報告している間に、宮廷への対応を手伝うつもりですので、ここに"
"残ろうと思っています。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:272
msgid "Understood. I'll leave you two to it."
msgstr "分かりました。では、その件はお二人にお任せすればよいですね。"

#. [message]: speaker=NF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:326
msgid ""
"Welcome, daughter. Pray tell, what brings you and such unusual company here?"
msgstr ""
"よく帰ったね、我が娘 Merynian よ。どうしたんだい、こんな珍しい方と一緒なの"
"は、なぜだい？"

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:330
msgid ""
"Good day, father, mother. We bring news of the last few months and the North."
msgstr ""
"ご機嫌いかが、お父さま、お母さま。この半年ほどの間に北で起きたことについて説"
"明しようと思って、それで来たのよ。"

#. [message]: speaker=NM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:334
msgid "Well then, do share."
msgstr "そうか、では話を聴こうじゃないか。"

#. [message]: speaker=EN
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:350
msgid "... And thus we stand before you."
msgstr "... ということで、我々は、こうして今ここにいるわけです。"

#. [message]: speaker=NF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:354
msgid ""
"Understood. We shall start mobilizing our forces. Until it is done, we "
"invite you to remain with us."
msgstr ""
"分かりました。我が軍隊の動員が始まりますな。それが完了するまでここで過ごせる"
"よう、あなたをご招待しよう。"

#. [message]: speaker=NM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:358
msgid ""
"Would you be so kind as to offer your friend a tour of the estate until "
"supper, daughter?"
msgstr ""
"Merynian、夕食まで時間があるから、ご友人に、敷地内をご案内してもらえるかし"
"ら？"

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:362
msgid ""
"Y—yes, I believe the grounds are worth a look. (<i>To Isandir</i>) Follow me!"
msgstr ""
"え、えぇ、この敷地内は、一見の価値が有るわよね。（<i>Isandir に向かって </"
"i>）どうぞ、こちらへ！"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:409
msgid ""
"We finally have the resources necessary to feed and house everyone for some "
"time."
msgstr ""
"やっと私たちは、当面の間、全員がひもじい思いをせずに過ごせるだけの資源を手に"
"入れたのです。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:413
msgid "That's great! We can finally think of something else."
msgstr "ほんとに凄いの！それで、ようやく他のことにも頭が回るようになったのよ。"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:417
msgid "Indeed... Well then, how is it going with Caror?"
msgstr "本当ねえ... それで、Caror とはどうなってるの？"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:421
msgid "Mother!"
msgstr "お母さま！"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:425
msgid "What? He seems to like you too."
msgstr "あら、彼もあなたのことが好きみたいよ。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:429
msgid "That's not the point!"
msgstr "今、その話はいいから！"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:444
msgid "I'm back."
msgstr "ただいま戻りました。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:448
msgid "Caror! How were the talks?"
msgstr "Caror！　話し合いはどうだった？"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:464
msgid "I see. What do you intend to do now?"
msgstr "あぁそういうことね。さ、これからどうするつもりなのかしら？"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:468
msgid "I don't know. I suppose I'll see if I can be of use anywhere."
msgstr "分かりません。どこかで役に立てるかどうか、見極めようと思っています。"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:472
msgid ""
"Things are finally under control here, go take a break, see your parents. "
"And take Sylindë with you, I want her out of my hair."
msgstr ""
"いろんなことがやっと落ち着いたのだから、少し体を休めて、ご両親にお会いになる"
"とよいわ。あ、Sylindë も一緒に連れて行ってくださいね。私、この子がいると邪魔"
"なのよ。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:476
msgid "Mother! Seriously?"
msgstr "お母さまったら！　本気なのですか？"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:480
msgid "U—uh... Yes I could."
msgstr "あ、、はい......そういたします。"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:484
msgid "Great! Well then, I'll see you two later."
msgstr "まあ素晴らしい！それじゃ私は、後ほど、ご両親にお会いするわね。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:525
msgid "You seem quite sad being here. Why is that?"
msgstr "ここにいると、とても寂しそうね。どうしたの？"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:529
msgid ""
"I'd much rather not have to bring the sad news. Though at the same time, who "
"else but me..."
msgstr "悲しい知らせは聞きたくないんです。でも、同時に、私以外の誰が......。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:533
msgid ""
"Oh... For what it's worth, I am truly sorry. I believe that, wherever your "
"friend is, he finds some joy in knowing that without him, nobody would have "
"survived this."
msgstr ""
"あぁ... 何より、本当に残念です。ご友人が何処にいようとも、ご自分なしでは誰一"
"人生き残れなかったとご存じですもの、きっとお喜びのことと思います。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:537
msgid ""
"Thanks... It's just... Turod's the one who was good with words... He'd know "
"what to say..."
msgstr ""
"有難う...でもね...Turod は口が達者なんです... あいつなら、何を言うべきか分"
"かっていただろうなって..."

#. [unit]: id=MK, type=Ancient Lich
#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#. [message]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:563
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:804
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:814
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:862
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:885
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1049
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1060
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1081
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1218
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1248
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:475
msgid "Mal Keshar"
msgstr "Mal Keshar"

#. [message]: speaker=MK
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:596
msgid "Orcish scum trampled the ground here and those weaklings fell to them."
msgstr "オークのカスは、ここの大地を踏みしめ、あの弱虫どもは奴らに倒された。"

#. [message]: speaker=MK
#: war_and_home/scenarios/20_Arrival_And_Warning.cfg:605
msgid ""
"This one still lives. We shall see how useful it is.\n"
"(<i>In an unearthly voice</i>) <i>A breath of unlife shall ease the way to "
"undeath.</i>\n"
"After all, why raise them when you can make sure they fall..."
msgstr ""
"こいつはまだ生きている。どの程度使い物になるか見物してやろう。\n"
"（<i>超自然的な声で </i>）<i>不死の息づかいは、不死への道を切り開くだろう。 "
"</i>\n"
"遂には、彼らが落ちてゆくことを見定められるときに、なぜ彼らを引き戻すのか..."

#. [scenario]: id=21_Morning_In_The_Night
#: war_and_home/scenarios/21_Morning_In_The_Night.cfg:7
msgid "Morning In The Night"
msgstr "夜に迎える朝"

#. [objective]: condition=win
#: war_and_home/scenarios/21_Morning_In_The_Night.cfg:23
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:23
msgid "End the turn"
msgstr "ターンを終了する"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/21_Morning_In_The_Night.cfg:94
msgid ""
"<i> “A breath of unlife shall ease the way to undeath.”</i>\n"
"\n"
"And so fell magic wove back a broken body, though not without imparting a "
"dark gift."
msgstr ""
"<i> \"不死の息づかいは、不死への道を切り開くだろう。\" </i>\n"
"\n"
"そうやって、魔術は壊れた体を組み上げていきましたが、闇の贈り物をも与えること"
"だったのです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/21_Morning_In_The_Night.cfg:99
msgid ""
"Chapter Twenty-One\n"
"<i>Morning In The Night</i>"
msgstr ""
"第21章\n"
"<i>夜に迎える朝 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/21_Morning_In_The_Night.cfg:142
msgid "W—what? How am I alive, I was dying?"
msgstr "ど、どうなったんだ？ 死にかけてたんだが、生き延びた？"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/21_Morning_In_The_Night.cfg:153
msgid "Is anyone else back up?... No... They still lie here..."
msgstr "他に誰か、戻ってるのか？... いや...横たわってる..."

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/21_Morning_In_The_Night.cfg:164
msgid "Are the others all right?... Let us hope we bought them enough time..."
msgstr ""
"他のみんなは、大丈夫だろうか？...十分に時間を稼げたことを願うしかない..."

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/21_Morning_In_The_Night.cfg:175
msgid ""
"In any case, remaining in the valley with the orcish patrols would be "
"certain death, I need to leave."
msgstr ""
"いずれにしても、このままオークの谷にいたら死ぬだけだ、ここを離れなければ。"

#. [scenario]: id=22_A_Desolate_Land
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:6
msgid "A Desolate Land"
msgstr "荒涼たる大地"

#. [scenario]: id=22_A_Desolate_Land
#. [scenario]: id=23_The_Monastery
#. [scenario]: id=25_A_Lone_Village
#. [scenario]: id=26_Encircled
#. [side]
#. [scenario]: id=29_A_Haven_Assaulted
#. [scenario]: id=30_Departure
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:70
#: war_and_home/scenarios/23_The_Monastery.cfg:75
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:86
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:87
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:99
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:95
#: war_and_home/scenarios/30_Departure.cfg:88
msgid "Rangers"
msgstr "レンジャーズ"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:109
msgid ""
"The kingdom needed to be warned in case the others had been stopped and, as "
"the southwestern passage through which they had fled was most likely "
"guarded, fleeing southeast was the only real option."
msgstr ""
"他の者たちに万が一のことがあった場合を考えると、王国に警告を出さなければなり"
"なせんでしたし、彼らが逃げた南西の通路は敵が警備している可能性が高いので、南"
"東に逃げるのが唯一の選択肢でした。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:112
msgid ""
"The valley was relatively easy to escape, with the orcish presence limited "
"to the occasional patrol which could be easily evaded by hiding beside a "
"tree.\n"
"\n"
"The land beyond proved less hospitable however, barren and monotonous, with "
"naught but a few small plants growing and no other sign of living beings, "
"save a few tracks here or there, or the remains of a long-abandoned hovel."
msgstr ""
"その渓谷は、逃走するのが比較的容易で、オークは時々巡回する程度でしたので、木"
"の脇に隠れれば簡単にかわせました。\n"
"\n"
"でも、その先の土地は快適とはいえず、不毛かつ単調で、小さな植物がわずかに生え"
"ている程度で生き物のいる様子はなく、あちらこちらに足跡は残っているか、または"
"長期間放置された小屋があるのみでした。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:117
msgid ""
"By the time I encountered a living being other than a starving wolf, I was "
"close to the breaking point, with little rations left and a mysterious pain "
"coursing through my body with every step I took.\n"
"\n"
"I was, by then, in a lifeless valley much like any other for many miles. "
"These lands truly seemed dead, as if some unknown power had decreed their "
"end in some forgotten age long past."
msgstr ""
"飢えた狼以外の生き物に遭遇した時には、もう限界に近い状態で、食料は底をつき、"
"歩くたびに体に奇妙な痛みが走りました。\n"
"\n"
"そのとき僕は、他の渓谷と同様、生気のない果てしない渓谷にいたのです。この土地"
"はまさに死んでいるかのようでした。まるで、忘れられた古の時代に、未知の力に"
"よって終わりを告げられたかのように。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:122
msgid ""
"Chapter Twenty-Two\n"
"<i>A Desolate Land</i>"
msgstr ""
"第22章\n"
"<i>荒涼たる大地 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:160
msgid ""
"And another valley, no doubt as empty as the last one, wonderful... And I "
"have almost no food left... I am going to die here, am I not..."
msgstr ""
"さっきまでの谷と同じように、この谷もまた間違いなく何もない、素敵なところだ"
"よ...。食料も尽きかけている... ここで死ぬしかなさそうだ、もう私は..."

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:165
msgid ""
"(<i>Sounds of battle can be heard from the south, metal clashes and great "
"warcries</i>)"
msgstr "(<i>南から戦闘音や金属の衝突音、そして盛大な鬨の声が聞こえます。 </i>)"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:169
msgid "Well, at least I might not do so alone..."
msgstr "まあ、少なくとも私一人では無理だとは思うが..."

#. [message]: speaker=OL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:192
msgid "Kill the humans!"
msgstr "人間どもを殺っちまえ！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:196
msgid "Orcs attacking people once more..."
msgstr "オークどもが、また人間を襲っている..."

#. [message]: speaker=OL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:200
msgid "Another human, kill him as well!"
msgstr "人間がもう一人いる、そいつも殺れ！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:204
msgid ""
"Please help us, we are pinned here and their reinforcements are coming! Some "
"of ours should be lurking near the northeastern camp, rally them!"
msgstr ""
"助けてくれ、我々はここに足止めされているし、奴らの援軍がやって来る！我々の兵"
"士が数名、北東の野営地の近くに潜んでいるはずだ、彼らを集めてほしい！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:214
msgid "I will assist!"
msgstr "お手伝いしよう！"

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:227
msgid ""
"After the actions of Mal Keshar, Turod's resistances and health will "
"progressively change over the next levels while he is not truly healed."
msgstr ""
"Mal Keshar の行動後、Turod の耐性と体力は次のレベルへと徐々に変化しますが、真"
"の意味で回復することはありません。"

#. [message]: speaker=OL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:242
msgid "Ha! Our reinforcements are here!"
msgstr "ハッハー！俺たちの援軍が来たぞ！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:246
msgid "Nooo! We'll never make it out now..."
msgstr "駄目だ！もう凌げそうにない..."

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:272
msgid ""
"Thank you for your help, my men and I appreciate it! My name is Haldar, what "
"might be yours?"
msgstr ""
"助けてくれてありがとう、部下も私も感謝している。私の名前は Haldar だ。君は？"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:276
msgid ""
"Turod. And likewise, for I would not have wished to meet them in battle "
"alone."
msgstr ""
"Turod だ。それと、もし私一人だったら、奴らに立ち向かうことは望まなかっただろ"
"う。"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:280
msgid ""
"Well then, Turod, I am glad to have met you. What brings you to these lands?"
msgstr ""
"まあとにかく Turod 、君に会えて嬉しいよ。この土地にはどんな理由で来たんだい？"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:284
msgid ""
"That is — <i>ouch!</i> — a long story. And though I will gladly share it, I "
"would rather do so while leaving this place, before their reinforcements "
"arrive."
msgstr ""
"それは ― <i>うっ！ </i> ― 長い話になるのだ。喜んでお話したいのだが、できれ"
"ば、彼らの援軍が到着する前にここから離れよう、その道すがら聞いてもらう方がい"
"いと思う。"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/22_A_Desolate_Land.cfg:288
msgid "Indeed, that would be the best course of action."
msgstr "確かに、それが最善の方法だな。"

#. [scenario]: id=23_The_Monastery
#: war_and_home/scenarios/23_The_Monastery.cfg:6
msgid "The Monastery"
msgstr "修道院"

#. [objective]: condition=win
#: war_and_home/scenarios/23_The_Monastery.cfg:20
msgid "Clear the monastery"
msgstr "修道院を確保する（修道院に入る）"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/23_The_Monastery.cfg:129
msgid ""
"While we hurried away, Haldar and I swapped tales.\n"
"\n"
"He and his men act as protectors for the few villages in the region, helping "
"to take out whatever threatens the peace."
msgstr ""
"急いで立ち去る間、Haldar と僕はいろいろな話をしました。\n"
"\n"
"Haldar とその部下たちは、この地域のいくつかの村の守護者として平和を脅かすもの"
"を排除する手助けをしているのです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/23_The_Monastery.cfg:134
msgid ""
"In return I told him of our journey and subsequent flight. He seemed quite "
"interested by this tale and far more knowledgeable about elven society than "
"I was.\n"
"\n"
"He asked multiple times for details, most often regarding the druids, and I "
"shared what little I knew."
msgstr ""
"僕の方はというと、僕たち一行の旅とその後の脱出行について話しました。彼はこの"
"話にかなり興味を持ったようで、しかも、僕よりもエルフの社会について遥かに知識"
"がありました。\n"
"\n"
"彼は何度も詳細を尋ねてきたけれど、その多くはドルイドに関してで、僕は自分の"
"知っていることを少し話しました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/23_The_Monastery.cfg:139
msgid ""
"At one of their camps, some of their healers tried to help me with that "
"strange weakness I had, to no avail.\n"
"\n"
"Afterwards, he offered that I remain with them until their patrol was over, "
"and we would reach a wise man who could help and they would then lead me "
"back to the kingdom.\n"
"\n"
"I agreed and we proceeded to the next destination, a remote monastery nearby."
msgstr ""
"Haldar たちのキャンプの一つで、何人かの治療師が僕のこの奇妙な衰弱を救おうと手"
"を尽くしてくれたのですが、無駄でした。\n"
"\n"
"その後、Haldar は僕に、彼の部下たちの巡回警護が終わるまで同行してから後、救い"
"の手を差し伸べてくれる賢者の所へ行けば、彼らが僕を王国へ連れて行ってくれるだ"
"ろうと提案してきました。\n"
"\n"
"僕はそれに同意して、一行は次の目的地の、この近くの人里離れた修道院へと足を向"
"けたのでした。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/23_The_Monastery.cfg:146
msgid ""
"Chapter Twenty-Three\n"
"<i>The Monastery</i>"
msgstr ""
"第23章\n"
"<i>修道院 </i>"

#. [label]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/23_The_Monastery.cfg:166
msgid "Monastery"
msgstr "修道院"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/23_The_Monastery.cfg:172
msgid ""
"These orcs are already pillaging the monastery, we need to take them — "
"<i>ow</i> — out!"
msgstr ""
"このオークどもは既に修道院を略奪している、我々は奴らを ― <i>痛い... </i> ― 追"
"い出す必要がある！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/23_The_Monastery.cfg:176
msgid ""
"You are not getting any better, are you?... In any case, forward, push them "
"out before their reinforcements arrive!"
msgstr ""
"君はまだ体調が戻っていないようだが、違うか？... とにかく前進だ、奴らの援軍が"
"来る前に一掃するんだ！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/23_The_Monastery.cfg:202
msgid "No! We will never take it back now!"
msgstr "駄目だ！もう、取り返すことは不可能だ！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/23_The_Monastery.cfg:211
msgid "We have the monastery! Men, clear the rest while we head inside!"
msgstr "修道院を確保したぞ！男たちよ、私たちが中に入る間、残兵を一掃するんだ!"

#. [scenario]: id=24_A_Child_Of_Light
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:7
msgid "A Child of Light"
msgstr "光の子"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:129
msgid ""
"While the rest of the troops handled the orcs, Haldar, Wolfie and I headed "
"inside to rescue whomever we could."
msgstr ""
"部隊がオークを相手にしている間に Haldar とウルフ、そして僕が内部に侵入し、で"
"きるだけ多くの者たちを救出しました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:132
msgid ""
"Chapter Twenty-Four\n"
"<i>A Child of Light</i>"
msgstr ""
"第24章\n"
"<i>光の子 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:182
msgid ""
"There are many corpses around here, I fear it went poorly for the monks..."
msgstr ""
"この辺りは死体が多い、僧侶たちにとっては不本意だったのではないかと心配だ..."

#. [message]: speaker=WF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:186
msgid "<i>Awoooooooo!</i>"
msgstr "<i>アウーーーーー！ </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:190
msgid ""
"The scent of blood seems strongest forward. Perhaps some still live amongst "
"the corpses."
msgstr ""
"血の匂いが一番強く漂ってくるようだ。おそらく、死体の中には、まだ生きている者"
"がいる。"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:201
msgid "I fear none remain who yet draw breath... Monsters..."
msgstr ""
"私は、まだ息をしている者は、残っていないのではないか不安だ... モンスターども"
"め..."

#. [message]: race=orc
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:206
msgid "Die, human scum! You can't run any longer!"
msgstr "死ね、人間のクズ！もう逃げられないぞ！"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:210
msgid "Help, somebody, please!"
msgstr "助けて、誰か、お願い！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:239
msgid "You have murdered enough, now it is your turn!"
msgstr "お前は、もう十分に殺しを重ねてきただろう、今度はお前の番だ！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:284
msgid "Are you unharmed?"
msgstr "どうだい、怪我はないかな？"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:288
msgid ""
"Y—yes, I am all right, thanks to you... He—he would have killed me... Oh "
"lords...."
msgstr ""
"はい、大丈夫です、ありがとうございます...　か、彼に殺されるところでした... あ"
"あ、なんてこと......"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:292
msgid "(<i>To Turod</i>) I will go check the other rooms, take care of her."
msgstr "(<i>Turod に </i>) 他の部屋を確認してくるから、彼女のことは任せたよ。"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:313
msgid "(<i>Kneeling besides her</i>) Do you think you can walk?"
msgstr "(<i>Elaessa の横にひざまずき </i>) 歩けそうかい？"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:317
msgid "Oh lords, the orcs killed everyone... They are all gone..."
msgstr ""
"あぁ.. Turod 様、オークが皆を殺してしまった... みんな死んでしまいました..."

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:321
msgid "(<i>Hugging and trying to comfort her</i>) I—It'll be alright..."
msgstr "(<i>抱きしめて慰めようとする </i>) 大丈夫だからね..."

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/24_A_Child_Of_Light.cfg:325
msgid ""
"(<i>Crying in his arms</i>) Th—They are all dead... Nooo, everyone, why..."
msgstr ""
"(<i>腕の中で泣きながら </i>) みんな、死んじゃったんです... いやよ、みんな、ど"
"うして..."

#. [scenario]: id=25_A_Lone_Village
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:6
msgid "A Lone Village"
msgstr "孤立した村"

#. [objective]: condition=lose
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:21
msgid "The enemy controls most of the villages in the town"
msgstr "敵に殆どの村を占拠される"

#. [side]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:106
msgid "Villagers"
msgstr "村人たち"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:186
msgid ""
"While I tried to comfort Elaessa as best I could, Haldar searched the rest "
"of the monastery, in vain. There were no survivors.\n"
"\n"
"Outside, the men took care of the remaining orcs, though without finding any "
"priest either."
msgstr ""
"僕が Elaessa を精一杯慰めている間、Haldar は修道院の残りの部分を探したけれ"
"ど、虚しい結果となりました。生存者は、見つかりませんでした。\n"
"\n"
"修道院の外では、彼の手下たちが残りのオークを始末したが、司祭さえ見つからな"
"かったのです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:191
msgid ""
"Elaessa collapsed of exhaustion as soon as we emerged from the ruins. She "
"slept soundly for some time, though sadly the sight of her ruined home "
"cruelly dispelled any hope of this having been just a nightmare.\n"
"\n"
"While we all understood her sadness, none of us could bring back the dead, "
"and so we could do nothing but try and comfort her."
msgstr ""
"僕たちが遺跡から出るとすぐ Elaessa は疲れて倒れてしまいました。しばらくはぐっ"
"すりと眠っていましたが、我が家同然だった修道院が廃墟となった現実を目の当たり"
"にして、ただ悪夢を見ただけであってほしいという望みが、無残にも打ち砕かれてし"
"まっていました。\n"
"\n"
"彼女の悲しみはよく理解できるけれど、死者を蘇らせることは誰にもできない。そ"
"う、僕たちにできることは、ただ彼女を慰めることだけでした。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:196
msgid ""
"After this fateful stop, only one other remained before the end of this "
"patrol.\n"
"\n"
"A village to the west who we hoped had been spared Orcish raids."
msgstr ""
"この運命的な寄り道を終えて、この巡回警護が終了するまでにやり残したことが一つ"
"だけありました。\n"
"\n"
"西の方には、オークの襲撃を免れていてほしいと僕らが願っていた村があるのです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:201
msgid ""
"Chapter Twenty-Five\n"
"<i>A Lone Village</i>"
msgstr ""
"第25章\n"
"<i>孤立した村 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:220
msgid "We should arrive soon. Let us hope all is well."
msgstr "そろそろ到着するはずだ。順調にいくことを願おう。"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:224
msgid "Yes, it would be for the — <i>ouch!</i> — best."
msgstr "ああ、そうなれば......<i>痛い！ </i>最高だな。"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:228
msgid "That accursed illness is not letting up..."
msgstr "その呪われた病気は、よくならないな...。"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:232
msgid "W—What illness?"
msgstr "病気、というのは？"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:236
msgid "It is unimportant. Let us focus on ensuring the town is safe first."
msgstr "大したことではないよ。まずは町の安全を確保することに集中しよう。"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:240
msgid "That will take some time, the orcs are already here!"
msgstr "それには時間がかかるな。オークどもが、もうここに来ている！"

#. [message]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:244
msgid "We will follow your orders, just please help us!"
msgstr "ご命令に従いますので、どうか助けてください！"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:270
msgid "No! N—not them! Please lords, not them..."
msgstr "おやめください、彼らは！ お願いです、神様、彼らはお召しにならないで..."

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:289
msgid "No! They control most of the town, they will kill everyone!"
msgstr "なんてことだ！町の大部分が支配されてる、奴ら、皆殺しにするつもりだ！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:315
msgid "The town is secured, they will probably not attack for now."
msgstr "町の安全は確保した、今のところは攻撃してこないはずだ。"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:319
msgid ""
"Good, then we can rest awhile here and try to see if Elaessa can do "
"something for you with her magic that is beyond the rest of us."
msgstr ""
"よし、それなら、ここでしばらく休んで、Elaessa の魔法で君に何かできないか見て"
"みよう、彼女は、生き残った中で一番の魔術の使い手なんだ。"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:323
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:367
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:385
msgid "I will try."
msgstr "やってみます。"

#. [message]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:337
msgid ""
"Thank the lords for your protection, we would not have survived otherwise!"
msgstr ""
"お守りいただいたことに感謝いたします、きっと私たちは生き残れなかったことで"
"しょう！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:363
msgid ""
"No thanks are needed, we only did what was right. (<i>To Elaessa</i>) We "
"will stay for a few nights here, perhaps you can see if you can help Turod?"
msgstr ""
"礼などいらないよ、我々は正しいことを実行したまでのことさ。 (<i> Elaessa に向"
"かって </i>) 我々は数日ここに滞在するつもりだが、ひょっとすると、君の力で "
"Turod を助けられるかもしれんぞ、な？"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:373
msgid "We couldn't save any of them..."
msgstr "誰一人、救えませんでした..."

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:377
msgid "At least those who sheltered themselves survived..."
msgstr "少なくとも、避難した者たちは生き延びたよ..."

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/25_A_Lone_Village.cfg:381
msgid ""
"The orcs should be scared off, let us hope these people have time to "
"rebuild. (<i>To Elaessa</i>) We will stay for a few nights here, perhaps you "
"can see if you can help Turod?"
msgstr ""
"オークは撃退したはずだ、この人たちに再建の時間があることを祈ろう。"
"(<i>Elaessa に向かって </i>) 我々は数日ここに滞在するつもりだが、ひょっとする"
"と、君の力で Turod を助けられるかもしれんぞ、な？"

#. [scenario]: id=26_Encircled
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:6
msgid "Encircled"
msgstr "包囲されて"

#. [objective]: condition=win
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:20
msgid "Defeat any enemy leader"
msgstr "敵のリーダーの誰かを倒す"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:189
msgid ""
"Though she did all she could, Elaessa's powers proved insufficient. All we "
"learned was that there seemed to actually be something, and that it was "
"magical in origin, more a spell or a curse than a natural illness.\n"
"\n"
"Though this was quite distressing, Haldar seemed confident that a magician "
"friend at his base could take care of it."
msgstr ""
"Elaessa はできる限りのことをしましたが、その力では満足な結果は得られませんで"
"した。分かったことは、どうやら何かがあるらしいということと、それが魔術的なも"
"のであり、自然の病気というよりも呪文や呪いによるものだろうということでし"
"た。\n"
"\n"
"このことは非常に残念ではあったのですが、Haldar は、彼の本拠地にいる魔術師の友"
"人なら何とかできると確信しているようでした。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:194
msgid ""
"This was not our most pressing concern, however, for orcish forces had been "
"spotted heading to our location.\n"
"\n"
"The villagers had agreed to evacuate to Haldar's refuge and so his men led "
"them out.\n"
"\n"
"However, before his men could finish leaving, the orcs cut us off and "
"encircled the village."
msgstr ""
"しかし、それよりももっと急を要する出来ごとが起きていました。オークの軍隊がこ"
"ちらへ向かっていることが確認されたのです。\n"
"\n"
"村人たちは Haldar の避難所へ避難することに同意して、Haldar の部下が村人たちを"
"先導して連れ出しました。\n"
"\n"
"ところが、避難し終える前にオークによって遮られ、村は包囲されてしまったので"
"す。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:201
msgid ""
"Chapter Twenty-Six\n"
"<i>Encircled</i>"
msgstr ""
"第26章\n"
"<i>包囲されて </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:231
msgid ""
"They truly have us surrounded... I don't want to end up in their hands... "
"Please, lords..."
msgstr ""
"あの者たちは本当に私たちを包囲しています... 彼らの手に落ちたくはありませ"
"ん... どうかお願いです、Turod 様..."

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:235
msgid "Don't worry, we'll get through it."
msgstr "心配いらない、我々は必ず乗り切ることができる。"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:239
msgid ""
"We just need to kill one of their leaders. That will create an opening and "
"we will then be able to evade the rest."
msgstr ""
"奴らのリーダーの一人を殺しさえすればいい。そうすれば隙が生まれて、残りの奴ら"
"からも逃れられるはずだ。"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:254
msgid "No! There are even more of them!"
msgstr "駄目だ！　奴ら、どんどん増える！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:263
msgid "We have our opening! Hurry, everyone, we'll cover the retreat!"
msgstr "突破口ができたぞ！ みんな急ぐんだ！ 退路を確保するんだ！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:275
msgid ""
"The rest of the men are out, we can run! Let's— ouch! (<i>He doubles over in "
"pain</i>)"
msgstr ""
"残りの者たちは外に出た。我々も走るぞ！ さあ ― 痛い！（<i>痛みが倍増して襲って"
"きました </i>）"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:279
msgid "No, the curse is getting worse!"
msgstr "いけません、呪いが悪化しています！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:283
msgid "Hurry on, I'll be fine!"
msgstr "急ぐんだ、私は大丈夫だ！"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:287
msgid "No you won't! I—I don't want others to die again!"
msgstr ""
"いいえ、大丈夫な筈がありません！ 私は ― 私はもう誰にも死んでもらいたくないの"
"です！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/26_Encircled.cfg:291
msgid "We'll rejoin the men later! Wolfie, carry him!"
msgstr "我々は後で仲間たちと合流することにしよう！ Wolfie 、彼を運ぶんだ！"

#. [scenario]: id=27_Into_The_Dark
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:6
msgid "Into The Dark"
msgstr "闇の中へ"

#. [objective]: condition=win
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:21
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:521
msgid "Escape the orcs"
msgstr "オークから逃れる"

#. [note]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:28
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:532
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:666
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1360
msgid ""
"Movement cost on normal cave terrain is reduced to 1 for all your units."
msgstr "味方ユニットは、洞窟内での移動コストが１に減ります。"

#. [note]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:31
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:535
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1363
msgid "The enemy monsters have a zone of control even if they are level 0."
msgstr "敵のモンスターたちは、レベル0であっても ZOC を持っています。"

#. [side]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:145
msgid "Monsters"
msgstr "モンスター"

#. [side]
#. [unit_type]: id=Remnant, race=undead
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:161
#: war_and_home/units/Remnant.cfg:7
msgid "Remnant"
msgstr "Remnant"

#. [side]
#. [side]: id=UL1, type=Revenant
#. [side]: id=UL2, type=Revenant
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:169
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:158
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:175
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:197
msgid "Undead"
msgstr "アンデッド"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:179
msgid ""
"Haldar and Elaessa, assisted by Wolfie, carried me out of there and managed "
"to evade the orcish pursuers, settling in a cave to the south-east for "
"refuge."
msgstr ""
"Haldar と Elaessa は、Wolfie に手助けしてもらって僕をそこから運び出し、オーク"
"の追っ手たちから何とか逃れて、南東の洞窟へと避難したのです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:182
msgid ""
"By that point, I had already fainted as the pain kept on rising. I would "
"soon become quite feverish as the curse seemed to come into its own."
msgstr ""
"その時点で、僕の痛みは更に酷くなっており、そのせいで既に気を失っていたので"
"す。やがて僕の体は、かなり発熱していました。きっと呪いが本性を現しだしたので"
"しょう。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:185
msgid ""
"Though Elaessa did her best to help me, there was little she could do apart "
"from watching over me while I drifted in and out of consciousness."
msgstr ""
"僕を助けようと Elaessa は懸命に尽力してくれましたが、僕の意識が混濁している状"
"態では、見守る以外に為すすべはありませんでした。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:188
msgid ""
"When I finally awoke, Haldar had left to scout the surroundings and had "
"taken Wolfie with him, leaving only Elaessa in the cave, besides me."
msgstr ""
"ようやく僕が目を覚ましたとき、Haldar は周囲の偵察のため外出しており、Wolfie "
"を同行させていました。Elaessa だけは洞窟に残っていて、僕の傍にいたのです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:191
msgid ""
"Chapter Twenty-Seven\n"
"<i>Into The Dark</i>"
msgstr ""
"第27章\n"
"<i>闇の中へ </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:253
msgid "Turod, you are awake! We were so worried, you were growing quite ill."
msgstr ""
"Turod 様、意識が戻ったのですね！とても心配していたのです、ほんとに具合が悪く"
"なってらしたのですよ。"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:257
msgid ""
"Apologies for the fright, and thank you for your concern... Where are we? Is "
"it Haldar's refuge?"
msgstr ""
"怖がらせてしまって申し訳ない。それと、心配してくれて感謝するよ... ここはどこ"
"なんだ？ Haldar の隠れ処かい？"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:261
msgid ""
"No, this is just a cave for shelter. Haldar went out — <i>yaawn</i> — to "
"scout... —Sorry for that..."
msgstr ""
"いいえ、ここは避難するために入った、ただの洞窟です。Haldar は -- <i>フアァ～"
"（あくび） </i> -- 偵察に... す、すみません..."

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:265
msgid ""
"It's not a problem, you seem to be in need of rest. I will take the watch "
"until he returns."
msgstr ""
"かまわないさ、君も体を休めたほうが良さそうだ。Haldar が戻るまで私が見張りをし"
"よう。"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:269
msgid "Th—Thank you very much... <i>Zzz</i>..."
msgstr "あ、ありがとうございま..す.. <i>Zzz </i>..."

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:273
msgid ""
"<i>She must have been really tired... I'll get her a blanket for now...</i>"
msgstr ""
"<i>よほど疲れていたに違いないな... とりあえず彼女に掛ける毛布でも探してこよ"
"う... </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:281
msgid "T—Turod? What is happening?"
msgstr "Turod 様、一体何が起きているのですか？"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:285
msgid "There are orcs close to the entrance. We need to prepare to leave."
msgstr "オークがここの入り口付近にいるんだ。立ち去る準備をしなければならん。"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:289
msgid "Where is Haldar?"
msgstr "Haldar は、どこに？"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:293
msgid ""
"Not back yet... And he won't be able to reach us through this entrance with "
"the orcs in the way. For now, let us wait and see if they come in."
msgstr ""
"まだ戻っていない... それに、このままオークが入り口にいたのでは戻っては来れま"
"い。ひとまず、奴らが入ってくるのを待ってみよう。"

#. [message]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:300
msgid "Sniff sniff... Smells like humans... they're inside!"
msgstr "<i>クンクン...クンクン... </i> 人間の匂いがするぞ...奴ら、この中だ！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:338
msgid "We have to go into the caves, now!"
msgstr "洞窟の中に入らなければ、さあ！"

#. [message]: speaker=OL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:369
msgid "Catch 'em and kill 'em!"
msgstr "奴らをとっ捕まえて、殺せ！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:507
msgid ""
"This detour to evade the patrols was far too long... We have to find Turod "
"and Elaessa and get away from here!"
msgstr ""
"あの監視を避けて迂回したのが遠すぎたな... Turod とElaessa を探し出してここか"
"ら逃げ出さないと！"

#. [message]: speaker=WF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:511
msgid "Woof woof!"
msgstr "ウ～ ガルー！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:515
msgid ""
"I know we need to hurry, but we must still be careful of monsters in these "
"caves!"
msgstr ""
"分かってるさ、急がないとな。でも、この洞窟のモンスターどもには注意しないとい"
"かんぞ！"

#. [objective]: condition=win
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:525
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:659
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1353
msgid "Reunite the two groups"
msgstr "2つのグループが再会する"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:591
msgid "Turod and Elaessa! You got this far, within the tunnels?"
msgstr "Turod と Elaessa じゃないか！よくここまで来れたな、洞窟にいたのか？"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:595
msgid ""
"(<i>Dragging Turod</i>) Yes, but please help, something happened and Turod's "
"curse was lifted but his wounds returned!"
msgstr ""
"(<i> Turod を引き摺りながら </i>) ええ、でも手助けをお願いします、何かが起き"
"て Turod 様の呪いは解けたんですけど、傷が、またぶり返してしまったの！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:599
msgid ""
"Follow me, I know the way forward. We will lose whoever is following us on "
"our way to my friend. He'll be able to help, he can handle these wounds!"
msgstr ""
"私について来い、俺はこの道のことはよく知ってる。俺の友人のところに行く途中"
"で、どんな追手だろうが俺たちを見失うはずさ。そいつなら Turod を救える、その傷"
"を治せる！"

#. [message]: speaker=OL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:647
msgid "We have lost 'em, fall back and guard the entrance, they won't get out!"
msgstr ""
"奴らを見失っちまった、一旦戻って、入り口を警護しろ、奴らは外には出ないだろ"
"う！"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:651
msgid "We won't be able to get back... Please lords, help us find a way out."
msgstr ""
"私たち、もう後戻りはできませんよね... Turod様、どうか出口へ辿り着かせてくださ"
"い。"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:692
msgid ""
"There was a cave-in... The passage will take a long time to clear... But "
"there's no other way... I hope the others are all right..."
msgstr ""
"ここは陥没していたのか... 通り抜けるには時間が掛かりそうだが... これ以外に道"
"はない... 二人が無事だといいが..."

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:758
msgid "I—I feel wrong, something is happening to me!"
msgstr "何か ― 何か悪い予感が、悪いことが起きそうな予感がする！"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:767
msgid "Turod, w—what is it?"
msgstr "Turod 様、一体、どうなされたんですか？"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:796
msgid "Yiargh!"
msgstr "ウオォーー！"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:800
msgid "Nooo, Turod!"
msgstr "駄目だわ、Turod 様！"

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:806
msgid ""
"(<i>A dark voice booms in the cave</i>) Good, you finally fell. Now, take "
"her as your first minion!"
msgstr ""
"(<i>洞窟に響く暗い声 <i>) よしよし、ついに倒れたか。さあ、この女を最初の手下"
"として連れて行け！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:810
msgid "..."
msgstr "..."

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:816
msgid ""
"A fool who held on until the bitter end, pitiful. You are but a puppet now, "
"a thinking one perhaps, but a puppet nonetheless."
msgstr ""
"最後まで耐え抜いた愚か者よ、哀れなものだ。お前はもう、ただの操り人形となっ"
"た。考えることはできても、それでも操り人形に過ぎないのだ。"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:820
msgid "Aarrrgh!"
msgstr "アァァ....!"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:824
msgid ""
"Thank you for holding on until the end... Let us hope we shall have a better "
"fate one day..."
msgstr ""
"最後まで耐え抜かれたことに感謝いたします... いつの日か、もう少し良い運命の元"
"でお逢いしましょう..."

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:864
msgid ""
"Such sentimentality... Well then, let us bind her spirit to yours, that you "
"may remain together forever."
msgstr ""
"なんとも感傷的なことだ... いいだろう、お前たち二人の魂を結びつけてやろうでは"
"ないか。永遠に一緒になれるぞ。"

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:887
msgid "Good. Now, assemble an army and kill this orc scum!"
msgstr "よーし、ほれ、軍をなして、オークのクズどもを成敗せよ！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:897
msgid "I ... can't... hold on... sorry..."
msgstr "耐えられない... 私には、とても。すまない..."

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:901
msgid "Turod? Turod! — No, please! — Hold on!"
msgstr ""
"Turod 様？  Turod 様！— ダメです、いけません！ — しっかりしてください！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:905
msgid ""
"I already... cheated... death twice... I guess a... third time... was too "
"much... to ask for..."
msgstr ""
"これまで2度も騙されて、そのたびに死を味わってきた... そして、3度目... 今度は"
"もう..."

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:909
msgid "I am trying to heal you! Keep your eyes open, please!"
msgstr ""
"私の力で治せるか、力を尽くしているところです！目を開いたままでいてください！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:913
msgid "You were... really nice... I wish we'd had... met earlier..."
msgstr ""
"君は...本当に素晴らしい人だったよ... できることなら、君と... もっと早く出会い"
"たかった..."

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:922
msgid "Noo! No, lords, please no..."
msgstr "いけません、いけません、Turod 様！　お願いですから..."

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:967
msgid "There is nothing behind this shrine, it's just a cave—in..."
msgstr "この神殿の裏には、何もないな、ただ陥没した地盤があるだけだ..."

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:971
msgid ""
"It feels peaceful, like it was a place for people to take refuge, not "
"worship... In any case, what do we do now?"
msgstr ""
"ここは、安全な感じで、礼拝と言うより、まるで人々が避難するための場所だったよ"
"うな... ともかく、これからどういたしましょう？"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:975
msgid "We will see, I—I don't know yet..."
msgstr "見てみよう。私には、まだ良く分からないが..."

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:999
msgid ""
"(<i>He falls to the ground</i>) Oh lords, the pain! I—I feel wrong, "
"something is happening to me!"
msgstr ""
"(<i>Turod が地面に倒れ込む </i>) 何てことだ、痛みが走る！　何か ― 何か悪い予"
"感が、悪いことが起きそうな予感がする！"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1003
msgid "Turod, w—what is it? Oh no, the curse! It's taking effect!"
msgstr "Turod 様、一体どういうことです？ 何てこと、呪いが！ 遂に呪いが！"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1024
msgid "Thank the lords, this light just held it back!"
msgstr "主よ、感謝します、この光が、呪いを追い払ってくれました！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1028
msgid "I feel far better than before... But who did this?"
msgstr "以前よりも、ずっと素晴らしい気分だ... だが、こんなことを誰が？"

#. [message]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1051
msgid ""
"(<i> A fell voice comes out of the dark spirit</i>) You only lived through "
"the power of the dark! This insignificant obstacle changes nothing, accept "
"your fate!"
msgstr ""
"(<i>闇の精霊から悪の声が聞こえてくる </i>) お前は闇の力で生きてきた、それだけ"
"のことだ！このような取るに足らぬ邪魔などでは何も変わらぬ、お前の運命を受け入"
"れよ！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1056
msgid "W—What are you, fell spirit!?"
msgstr "な、なんだお前は、悪霊か！？"

#. [message]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1062
msgid "The one who kept you alive, and the one you shall bow to!"
msgstr "お前の命を生かした者であり、お前が服従すべき者である！"

#. [message]: speaker=RT
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1077
msgid ""
"...This is a refuge for the wounded and suffering. You have no place here, "
"fell undead."
msgstr ""
"...ここは傷つき悩める者の避難所だ。お前たちの居場所は無い、悪しきアンデッド"
"よ。"

#. [message]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1083
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You are nothing more than a fading remnant of a long-lost soul! You have "
"almost no power left!"
msgstr ""
"お前こそ、もはや消えゆく魂の残り香に過ぎぬ！その力は、ほとんど残っておらぬ！"

#. [message]: speaker=RT
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1087
msgid ""
"They have held onto hope through terrible trials, it shall not be denied to "
"them before me!"
msgstr ""
"彼らは苦難を乗り越えて希望を持ち続けてきたのだ、彼らには、私の前で否定される"
"ようなことなど何もないであろう！"

#. [message]: speaker=RT
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1172
msgid ""
"I may have little power left, but I shall not stand by idly... They will not "
"be left on their own!"
msgstr ""
"私の力は僅かしか残っていないが、ただ黙って見ておくことなどしない... 彼らは、"
"決して見捨てられることはない！"

#. [effect]: type=arcane
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1187
msgid "echo of hope"
msgstr "希望の響き"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1210
msgid "I feel better than before and — <i>why is my sword glowing!?</i>"
msgstr ""
"以前よりも、素晴らしい気分だ、それに... <i>なぜ、私の剣が輝いているのだ？ </"
"i>"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1214
msgid "He gave us his blessing, that we might beat this undead!"
msgstr ""
"あの方が、聖なる恵みを与えてくださったのです！ このアンデッドを倒せるように！"

#. [message]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1220
msgid "Then try, poor fools, for all your efforts will be for naught!"
msgstr ""
"試してみるがよい、哀れな愚か者たちよ。そうして、その努力は、無に帰するのだ！"

#. [message]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1250
msgid ""
"Fool, that pitiful remnant did not have enough power to truly heal you, you "
"will die of your wounds!"
msgstr ""
"愚か者め、あの憐れむべき残骸は、お前を真に治癒させるに足る力など持っていな"
"かった、お前はその傷によって死ぬことになる！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1275
msgid "Ouch!"
msgstr "痛い！"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1279
msgid "Turod, are you alright? You seem heavily wounded!"
msgstr "Turod 様、大丈夫ですか？傷がとても深いようです！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1283
msgid "I fear that fell monster spoke the truth..."
msgstr ""
"あの悪しきモンスターの語ったことは真実なのではないかと、それが怖いのだ..."

#. [message]: speaker=RT
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1297
msgid ""
"I sadly indeed had no power left, but take heart, for your way out is "
"close... As a parting gift, take the memories of this battle and remember, "
"whenever you face the dark again, bring your light to bear and all shall be "
"well."
msgstr ""
"悲しいことに、もう私の力は残っていない。だが、勇気を持て、出口は近い...　餞別"
"に、この戦いの記憶を持ち帰れ。そして忘れるな、再び闇に対峙したとき、光で立ち"
"向かえば、全てのことはうまくいくだろう。"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1347
msgid "The way behind the statue is clear, let's go!"
msgstr "像の裏側の道には誰もいません、さあ行きましょう！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/27_Into_The_Dark.cfg:1380
msgid "The cave-in cleared itself magically... Let us advance cautiously..."
msgstr "陥没部分が魔法のように勝手に修復したぞ... さあ、注意して先に進もう..."

#. [scenario]: id=28_Back_From_The_Brink
#: war_and_home/scenarios/28_Back_From_The_Brink.cfg:5
msgid "Back From The Brink"
msgstr "死の淵からの生還"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/28_Back_From_The_Brink.cfg:67
msgid ""
"Though the intervention of the benevolent spirit had lifted the curse, the "
"fell spectre had still left darkness in its wake."
msgstr ""
"慈悲深い精霊が介入したことで、呪いは解けましたが、悪しき化け物は、闇の残滓と"
"言えるものをいまだ残していました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/28_Back_From_The_Brink.cfg:70
msgid ""
"I had rapidly fallen unconscious once more, and Haldar and Elaessa had to "
"carry me out of the tunnels."
msgstr ""
"僕は、またもや突如、意識を失ってしまいました。Hadlar と Elaessa は、僕を担い"
"で洞窟の外へと運び出さねばなりませんでした。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/28_Back_From_The_Brink.cfg:73
msgid ""
"Chapter Twenty-Eight\n"
"<i>Back From The Brink</i>"
msgstr ""
"第28章\n"
"<i>死の淵からの生還 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/28_Back_From_The_Brink.cfg:96
msgid "... Ugh ... Where am I?"
msgstr "ウッ... ここはどこだ？"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/28_Back_From_The_Brink.cfg:100
msgid ""
"Oh, Turod, you woke up! Haldar's friend healed you, you should be all right "
"now!"
msgstr ""
"あっ、 Turod 様、目が覚めましたね！ Haldar のお友達が治療しくれたのです、もう"
"大丈夫ですわ！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/28_Back_From_The_Brink.cfg:114
msgid "I am grateful for his help... How long was I asleep?"
msgstr "その人の助けに感謝しなければ... 私はどのくらい眠っていたんだろう？"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/28_Back_From_The_Brink.cfg:118
msgid ""
"Only about a day... I—I kept watch in case you reacted badly to the "
"treatment... They both said you should rest a few more days and then they "
"would help you reach Wesnoth."
msgstr ""
"およそ一日です... わ、私は、治療を受けるあなたが痛そうに反応する様子を、ずっ"
"と見守っておりました... あと数日は体を休めたほうがよいと、二人が言っていまし"
"た。そうしたら、Wesnoth へ行くのを手伝ってくれるそうです。"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/28_Back_From_The_Brink.cfg:122
msgid ""
"Well then, thank you as well... And, as for Wesnoth, if you don't really "
"know what to do now... well, you could always go there as well."
msgstr ""
"そうか、君にも感謝しなければならないね... それと、その Wesnoth の件だけど、も"
"し君自身はどうすべきか迷っているなら... うん、君も一緒に来るといいんじゃない"
"かな。"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/28_Back_From_The_Brink.cfg:126
msgid ""
"Really? I—I have never been there. I spent my whole life in the monastery... "
"A—And anyway, I wouldn't know where to go once there, though..."
msgstr ""
"本当ですか？ わ、私はまだ行ったことがなくて。生まれてからずっと修道院で過ごし"
"てきたもので...  行ってみたとしても、その後どうすればいいかすら分からないです"
"し..."

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/28_Back_From_The_Brink.cfg:130
msgid ""
"There are many people in need of a healer there, and I would probably need "
"help as well."
msgstr "治癒者を必要とする人は大勢いるよ。それに、私だって助けてほしい。"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/28_Back_From_The_Brink.cfg:134
msgid "T—Then I shall be happy to come along!"
msgstr "そ、それなら、私は、喜んでご一緒いたします！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/28_Back_From_The_Brink.cfg:138
msgid ""
"Great! Now, I should probably go give my thanks to Haldar and his friend."
msgstr ""
"よかった！さあ、私は Haldar と、その友人にお礼を言いに行かなきゃならないね。"

#. [scenario]: id=29_A_Haven_Assaulted
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:6
msgid "A Haven Assaulted"
msgstr "急襲された安息の地"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:141
msgid ""
"Haldar's friend was an odd sort, an old mage named Elzear who spoke little, "
"though he seemed always quite confident and assured in his actions.\n"
"\n"
"Elzear had chosen to live in these parts to try and help them regrow, so "
"desolate he found them. He had decided he would make them green and full of "
"life by planting trees and flowers, one valley after another."
msgstr ""
"Haldar の友人は Elzear という風変わりな老魔術師で口数は少なく、しかし、行動す"
"るときは常に自信と確信を持っているようでした。\n"
"\n"
"Elzear は、この地に住みつき、目の前の荒れ果てた大地を再生させる手助けをしよう"
"と考えたのでした。緑豊かにしようと決心し、谷から谷へ木や花を植えて、生き物で"
"満たしていくのだと。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:146
msgid ""
"He had already achieved this with this one where he had established himself, "
"as it had become quite lively, with many animals in its vibrant forests.\n"
"\n"
"Elaessa spent some time with him on a few of his planting trips while I "
"recovered, and he taught her a little of his magic in return."
msgstr ""
"彼が定住したこの地は既に彼の理想を実現していて、鮮やかな緑の森に多くの動物が"
"生息し、生気溢れる様子でした。\n"
"\n"
"Elaessa は私が回復するまでの間、幾度か彼の植林の仕事にも同行していて、そのお"
"礼代わりに彼の魔法を少し教えてもらっていました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:151
msgid ""
"When I finally finished healing, Haldar showed me around the small village "
"that had been growing in the wake of Elzear's efforts to bring back life to "
"this place.\n"
"\n"
"It seemed, much like the rest of the valley, sheltered from the desolation "
"of the neighbouring lands. The villagers were quite happy to see us and "
"amongst them I recognized some of the warriors that had fought beside us in "
"the previous battles, as well as some refugees from the evacuated villages, "
"building themselves a new life."
msgstr ""
"ようやく僕の治療が終わると、Haldar は Elzear がこの地に生命を取り戻そうと努力"
"し結実した一つ、拓けつつある小さな村へと案内してくれました。\n"
"\n"
"そこは、この谷の他の地域と同じように、近隣の寂寞とした土地から守られているよ"
"うでした。村人たちは僕たちとの出会いを喜んでいました。また、その中には、前の"
"戦いで共に戦った戦士たちもいましたし、かつて襲われた村から避難し、ここで新生"
"活を築き直そうとしている難民の姿もありました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:156
msgid ""
"I rapidly became well enough to travel and we soon decided to depart, that "
"we might reach Wesnoth as fast as possible.\n"
"\n"
"However, that plan did not take into account some unwelcome visitors..."
msgstr ""
"まもなく僕は旅立てるほど回復して、速やかに Wesnoth に到着できるよう、出発する"
"ことにしました。\n"
"\n"
"ただ、その計画に、招かれざる客についての想定はありませんでした..."

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:161
msgid ""
"Chapter Twenty-Nine\n"
"<i>A Haven Assaulted</i>"
msgstr ""
"第29章\n"
"<i>急襲された安息の地 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:182
msgid "No, Elzear!"
msgstr "死ぬな、Elzear ！"

#. [message]: speaker=OM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:195
msgid ""
"There are some within the forests who remember the times before the green. "
"They do not look kindly upon those who would bring these back."
msgstr ""
"森の中には、緑が茂る前の頃の記憶を持つ者もおる。そうした者たちは、この地を以"
"前のようにしようとする者たちを好意的には見ておらぬ。"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:305
msgid ""
"We seem to have quite an unexpected visit... Pray tell, what brings you here?"
msgstr "いきなりやってくるとは。教えてくれないか、何をしに来たんだ？"

#. [message]: speaker=BL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:309
msgid ""
"We have followed some of yours and that led us right 'ere! Now, time to take "
"over this place and live like kings, isn't that right, boys?"
msgstr ""
"オマエらの仲間のあとをつけてたら、ここに来ちまったのよ！さてと、ここを占領し"
"て王様気分で暮らす時がきたようだ。チンピラども、そう思うよな？"

#. [message]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:314
msgid "That's right, boss!"
msgstr "その通りっす、大頭領！"

#. [message]: speaker=BL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:318
msgid ""
"We'll have a bunch of servants, plenty of animals to hunt and a whole lot of "
"tinder to burn while we wait for the orcs to leave!"
msgstr ""
"奴隷どもも山ほどいるし、狩る動物も山ほどいる、周りも山だらけだがな！オークが"
"いなくなるのを待つ間は、燃やす火種も<b>山ほど</b>あるってわけだ！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:322
msgid ""
"No you will not. Turod, mobilize the fighters in the village, Wolfie and I "
"will slow them at the river!"
msgstr ""
"いや、そいつは間違いだ。Turod 、村の戦士を出動させるんだ。Wolfie と私は川で足"
"止めする！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:326
msgid "Understood, I'll get them ready — (<i>To Elaessa</i>) Ready to fight?"
msgstr "よし、準備しよう — （<i>Elaessa に </i>）戦う準備はいいか？"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:330
msgid ""
"Y—yes, and with the spells Elzear taught me, I'll be able to help far more "
"than before!"
msgstr "は、はい、Elzear から教わった呪文で、前よりもずっとお役に立てますよ！"

#. [message]: speaker=BL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:340
msgid ""
"Fools, you struggled for too long, the orcs have probably already noticed "
"your presence!"
msgstr ""
"バカめ、時間を掛けてきたんだ、オークはもうオマエらがいることに気づいてるだろ"
"うよ！"

#. [message]: speaker=BL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:352
msgid "No, this can't— uurgh..."
msgstr "くそっ、あり得んだろ...うう..."

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/29_A_Haven_Assaulted.cfg:359
msgid "Should the rest of you surrrender, you will be treated well."
msgstr "貴様たちが降伏するなら、それなりの扱いで迎えてくれるだろうよ。"

#. [scenario]: id=30_Departure
#: war_and_home/scenarios/30_Departure.cfg:5
msgid "Departure"
msgstr "出立のとき"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/30_Departure.cfg:116
msgid ""
"After this incident, we decided it was more than time for us to depart and "
"head to Wesnoth.\n"
"\n"
"We rapidly finished preparing and then headed to Elzear's house to begin "
"leaving."
msgstr ""
"この出来事があり、僕たちは Wesnoth へ向けてそろそろ出発せねばと決めたので"
"す。\n"
"\n"
"皆、急いで支度して Elzear 宅へ向かい、旅立つ手筈を整え始めました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/30_Departure.cfg:121
msgid ""
"Chapter Thirty\n"
"<i>Departure</i>"
msgstr ""
"第30章\n"
"<i>出立のとき </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/30_Departure.cfg:161
msgid "So, are you both ready?"
msgstr "さあ、2人とも準備はいいかい？"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/30_Departure.cfg:165
msgid "Yes!"
msgstr "大丈夫です！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/30_Departure.cfg:169
msgid ""
"Yes, and thank you for your help. I would have been long-dead without it."
msgstr ""
"できてるさ、それと、君の支援に感謝するよ。君無しでは、私は、とっくの昔に死ん"
"でいたことだろう。"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/30_Departure.cfg:173
msgid "It was no trouble and in any case you helped us in return."
msgstr ""
"大したことじゃないさ。まあ、そもそも、俺たちは君に助けてもらった、その御礼に"
"したことじゃないか。"

#. [message]: speaker=WF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/30_Departure.cfg:177
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:261
msgid "Woof!"
msgstr "ウ～ ガルー！"

#. [message]: speaker=OM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/30_Departure.cfg:181
msgid "... These gryphons will carry you four to Wesnoth."
msgstr ""
"... このグリフォンたちが 君たち４人を Wesnoth に連れて行ってくれるじゃろう。"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/30_Departure.cfg:185
msgid "Haldar, you are coming with us?"
msgstr "Haldar、私たちにご一緒してくださるの？"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/30_Departure.cfg:189
msgid ""
"Yes. After all, I did promise Turod. And in any case, the orcs' actions may "
"have endangered some people I care about. I'll go check up on them."
msgstr ""
"ああ、そういうことになった。Turod と約束したのさ。何にしろ、オークの動向次第"
"では、俺が面倒を見てる人たちを危険に晒してるかもしれないんだ。それを確かめな"
"いとな。"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/30_Departure.cfg:193
msgid ""
"Thank you very much to the both of you. Well then, let us ride the gryphons!"
msgstr "二人とも、本当にありがとう。さあ、グリフォンで空を駆けようじゃないか！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/30_Departure.cfg:208
msgid "Goodbye Elzear, see you soon."
msgstr "じゃあな、Elzear。 すぐ戻ってくるからな。"

#. [message]: speaker=OM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/30_Departure.cfg:212
msgid "Goodbye, enjoy the flight."
msgstr "また後でな、空の旅を楽しみたまえ。"

#. [scenario]: id=31_Return_To_Wesnoth
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:5
msgid "Return To Wesnoth"
msgstr "Wesnoth への帰還"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:105
msgid ""
"Flying is, quite honestly, an experience without compare. Once the initial "
"moments of fear are over, and you start opening your eyes, the feeling of "
"freedom and the beauty of the view is something that I had never even "
"imagined before."
msgstr ""
"空を飛ぶ、というのは、まさに比類なき体験です。最初に飛び立つときの恐怖心を凌"
"ぎさえすれば、そのあと目を開けたときに感じられる自由さと景観の美しさと言った"
"ら、それまでの想像を遥かに超えるものなのだから。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:108
msgid ""
"With the gryphons' help, we rapidly arrived in Soradoc, where we would warn "
"the realm if the others hadn't made it out and then join the fight once "
"more.\n"
"\n"
"However, we had a far more interesting meeting before even entering the city "
"itself."
msgstr ""
"グリフォンの助けで、あっという間に Soradoc に到着しました。Sradoc で他の者た"
"ちが脱出できない場合には、本国に連絡し、再び戦闘に参加することになるでしょ"
"う。\n"
"\n"
"しかし僕たちは、その市街地へ入る前に更に興味深い出会いを果たすことになったの"
"です。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:113
msgid ""
"Chapter Thirty-One\n"
"<i>Return To Wesnoth</i>"
msgstr ""
"第31章\n"
"<i>Wesnoth への帰還 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:185
msgid "Flight is really wonderful, isn't it?"
msgstr "空を飛ぶって、本当に素敵なことですね。ですよね？"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:189
msgid ""
"Yes, it was quite enjoyable. Though I must admit, I do also enjoy being back "
"on solid ground!"
msgstr ""
"ああ、本当に楽しかったよ、それは間違いなけれど、硬い大地に足が着いたときの喜"
"びもまた一入だよ！"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:193
msgid "So, this is what the main towns in the realm of Wesnoth look like..."
msgstr "ところで、 Wesnoth 領の主要な町というのは、こんな感じなのですね..."

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:197
msgid ""
"I forget, you never really saw it. This is not its greatest city, for "
"Soradoc is eclipsed by the likes of Dan Tonk, or the capital Weldyn, but it "
"is still where I was born."
msgstr ""
"あぁ忘れていた、君はまだ見たことがなかったんだったね。いや、ここが最大の町と"
"いうわけではないんだ。Soradoc は Dan Tonk や 首都 Weldyn に資源を持っていかれ"
"るからね。でも、ここが私の生まれ故郷であることは間違いない。"

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:201
msgid "You were born here?"
msgstr "ここでお生まれに？"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:205
msgid ""
"Yes. I can give you a tour later if you want, though first we shall have to "
"get in."
msgstr ""
"そうさ。もし良ければ、あとで君を少し案内しよう、ともかく、先ずは中に入ろう。"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:209
msgid "Is that a refugee camp? Perhaps your friends made it."
msgstr "あれは避難用の野営地か？おそらく、君の友人たちが作ったんだろうな。"

#. [message]: type=Spearman
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:242
msgid "Halt, who goes there?"
msgstr "止まれ。誰だ、何者だ？"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:246
msgid ""
"A soldier of Wesnoth who was part of an army sent North and who returns with "
"news... Though, looking around, I would assume at least part of it has "
"already been received."
msgstr ""
"北方へ派遣された軍隊の一員たる Wesnoth の兵士が、報せを持って帰還した... だ"
"が、周囲の様子からすると、少なくともその報告の一部は既に受け取られているよう"
"だ。"

#. [message]: type=Spearman
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:250
msgid ""
"Understood, you may follow me inside the town to give your report. Your "
"friends will be housed while you do so."
msgstr ""
"了解しました、貴殿は、その報告を携えて、私に付いて町の中へどうぞ。ご友人たち"
"は、その間、別室でお待ちいただきます。"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:265
msgid "...Wolfie? ...Haldar?"
msgstr "あら、 ...Wolfie ？ ...Halder じゃない?"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:269
msgid "Anówien?"
msgstr "Anówien ？"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:278
msgid "Haldar! How did you get here?"
msgstr "Halder！ ここまで、どうやって？"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:282
msgid ""
"It is a long story... My companions are Turod, an officer of the Wesnothian "
"army and Elaessa, a priestess of the Light."
msgstr ""
"いろいろあって... Wesnoth 軍の将校 Turod と、光の魔術師 Elaessa も一緒なん"
"だ。"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:286
msgid "Turod... would you perhaps be friends with Caror, Merynian and Oweomyr?"
msgstr ""
"Turod も...　もしかすると Caror や Merynian、Oweomyr とも友人になれるんじゃな"
"いかしら？"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:290
msgid "Yes! Did they get back here? Is Caror alive?"
msgstr "おぅ！ 彼ら、ここに戻ってきたのかい？ Caror は無事か？"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:294
msgid ""
"All your friends are alive, they made it back here and are now back fighting "
"on the front, they made it out of Merlyc. As for Caror, however, that tale "
"is somewhat longer. (<i>To the guard</i>) They are allies of ours, I assume "
"no further escort is necessary."
msgstr ""
"お友だちは皆さん、ご無事で戻っていらして、今また最前線で戦ってらっしゃるわ。"
"Merlyc から抜け出せたのよ。Caror のことは、一言じゃ話せないわね。(<i>警護兵"
"に </i>）彼らは私たちの盟友なのよ、あとの護衛は不要よね。"

#. [message]: type=Spearman
#: war_and_home/scenarios/31_Return_To_Wesnoth.cfg:298
msgid "Indeed, I shall leave you to your reunion."
msgstr "ええ確かに。再会のお時間をごゆっくりとどうぞ。"

#. [scenario]: id=32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:6
msgid "Like Waves Upon The Rocks"
msgstr "岩を削る波濤の如く"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:132
msgid ""
"Anówien told us of how her people and Caror had evaded the orcs by waiting "
"them out in the North and then sailing down south to end up besides "
"Merynian, Oweomyr, Lumiclya and Isandir, taking back Merlyc from bandits "
"before evacuating over the Great River.\n"
"\n"
"Now, after having rested a little, they were leading the kingdom's "
"counterattack with a force of hardened veterans from the previous expedition "
"and some of the elves of Lintanir, as their main army."
msgstr ""
"Anówien は、彼女と Caror が北方でオークを待ち伏せてから南下し、Merynian、"
"Oweomyr、Lumiclya、Isandir と合流し、大いなる川を越えて避難する前に MerLyc を"
"盗賊から奪還したことを僕らに話してくれました。\n"
"\n"
"さて、彼らは少し休憩してから、前回の遠征で鍛えられたベテラン軍と Lintanir の"
"エルフの一部を主力軍として、王国の反撃を率いていました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:138
msgid ""
"They were fighting in the region of Carcyn, pushing back the orcish forces "
"there and trying to break through towards Elensefar to relieve its defenders "
"from the siege they were facing.\n"
"\n"
"In parallel, Wesnoth's defences were under great pressure at the ford of "
"Abez, where the orcs were making repeated assaults to defeat its defenders "
"and reach the realm's heartlands."
msgstr ""
"彼らは Carcyn 地方で戦闘中でしたが、オーク軍を押し戻して、包囲されている状況"
"から Eelensefar を解放するために突破しようと試みていました。\n"
"\n"
"時を同じくして、Wesnoth の防衛隊は Abez の浅瀬で大きな圧力に晒されていまし"
"た。そこではオークが防衛隊を打ち破って国土の中心地に到達しようと、攻撃を繰り"
"返していたのです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:144
msgid ""
"The orcish attack had cut Wesnoth off from its main ally, Wesmere, as well "
"as its primary port, Elensefar. These maneuvers had put the kingdom on the "
"defensive but, though this loss of initiative was a problem, the counter-"
"offensive was on its way and had quite some potential.\n"
"\n"
"The main concern was the series of attacks on the ford of Abez and the "
"consequences should its defenders fall. Anówien agreed and was going to lead "
"some elvish and human reinforcements there. However, as they were mostly "
"fresh recruits, including the officers, she was in need of some veterans to "
"assist and proposed to the city's commander that I lead this force as well, "
"something to which he readily agreed."
msgstr ""
"オークの攻撃は、主要な同盟 Wesmere と、主要な港のある Elensefar から Wesnoth "
"を切り離してしまいました。これらの作戦によって Wesnoth 王国は守勢に立たされま"
"したが、主導権を失ったことには問題がありました。彼らからの反撃が開始され、か"
"なりの勢いを持っていました。\n"
"\n"
"僕の最大の懸念は、Abez の浅瀬への切れ間のない攻撃と、防衛隊が陥落した場合はど"
"うなるかでした。Anówien も同じ意見だったので、エルフと人間の援軍を何人か率い"
"て行くことになりました。しかし、将校を含めて殆どが新兵だったために彼女には数"
"名の古参兵の援助が必要で、僕がその部隊を率いることを町の司令官に提案しまし"
"た。司令官はあっさりと快諾してくれました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:150
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"And so we headed to the Ford, Haldar and Wolfie standing beside Anówien, "
"happy to be reunited, while Elaessa was with me at the head of the human "
"detachment. Though the situation was serious, with a great war firmly upon "
"us, I found solace in the fact that all my friends had survived the return "
"from the North with far less support than what they would now have. If we "
"had all survived that, we would probably survive the rest, would we not?"
msgstr ""
"こうして僕たちは浅瀬へ向かい、Haldar と Anówien の隣りにいる Wolfie とも再会"
"を喜びあいました。そして Elaessa は僕とともに人間族の分隊の先頭に立ちました。"
"しかし、状況は深刻で、大きな戦いが目の前に迫っていましたが、北方からの帰還の"
"際には友人たちがみんな今より遥かに少ない援軍のもと生き延びたという事実に元気"
"づけられました。もし僕たち全員が北方からの帰還を生き延びられるなら、おそらく"
"この先もうまくいくでしょう。そう思いませんか？"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:153
msgid ""
"Chapter Thirty-Two\n"
"<i>Like Waves Upon The Rocks</i>"
msgstr ""
"第32章\n"
"<i>岩を削る波濤の如く </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=HG1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:231
msgid "Hold the line, push them back!"
msgstr "戦線を死守し、奴らを押し返せ！"

#. [message]: speaker=B1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:235
msgid "Forward! Kill them all and their realm will be ours!"
msgstr "前進だ！奴らを皆殺しにして、領土をぶん取れ！"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:239
msgid "It seems that we have arrived during an assault."
msgstr "どうやら、襲撃を受けてる最中に到着しちゃったみたいね。"

#. [message]: speaker=HG1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:243
msgid ""
"Reinforcements, finally!... Is that you, Turod? It seems reports of your "
"death were exaggerated."
msgstr ""
"援軍だぞ、遂に来たか！...　君は、Turod か？君が死んだという報告はデタラメだっ"
"たみたいだな。"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:247
msgid ""
"They were indeed, general Morain. In any case, we are here to provide "
"assistance."
msgstr ""
"確かにそうですね、Morain 将軍。とにかく、我々は支援のためにこちらへ参りまし"
"た。"

#. [message]: speaker=HG1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:251
msgid "Excellent. Help us push them back before their reinforcements arrive!"
msgstr "素晴らしい。奴らを押し返すのを手伝ってくれ、奴らの援軍が来る前にな！"

#. [message]: speaker=HG1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:266
msgid ""
"They still hold too much ground, their reinforcements will turn the tide!"
msgstr ""
"奴らは、そうとう地盤固めが強固なようだ。これで援軍まで来たら、戦いの流れが変"
"わってしまうだろう！"

#. [message]: speaker=B1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:277
msgid "Aargh... must... retreat!"
msgstr "うぐぐ.... 退却するしかねえ！"

#. [message]: speaker=HG1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:281
msgid "Good, press the advantage, they will be disorganized!"
msgstr "よーし、優位なままで押し切るぞ、奴らはもうガタガタ状態寸前だ！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:290
msgid "They have been driven back beyond the shore!"
msgstr "奴らを海岸線の彼方へ追いやったぞ！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:294
msgid "Understood, now we press on and rout them!"
msgstr "よし、押して押して押しまくって、奴らを総崩れにしてやるぞ！"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/32_Like_Waves_Upon_The_Rocks.cfg:298
msgid "Indeed, forward!"
msgstr "勿論ですわ、前進よ！"

# 検討
#. [scenario]: id=33_Cornered_And_Slain
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:6
msgid "Cornered and Slain"
msgstr "窮鼠に迫る"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:122
msgid ""
"While some of our cavalry harassed the retreating orcish forces, we met with "
"general Morain to plan our next move, as the orcish rout from the region had "
"opened new possibilities that could be quite interesting to exploit.\n"
"\n"
"We decided, as news came that the orcs' retreat took them towards Wesmere, "
"to head there and pincer them with the elvish forces that would no doubt be "
"defending the forest while leaving a small garrison here to help the defence "
"of the Ford."
msgstr ""
"騎馬隊の一部が退却するオーク軍を執拗に攻めている間、僕たちは Morain 将軍と次"
"の行動計画を立てようと相談していました。オークがこの地から退却すれば、非常に"
"興味深い展開へ持ち込める新たな可能性が考えられたからです。\n"
"\n"
"退却したオークが Wesmere へ向かっているという報せが入ったので、次のように決定"
"されました。この浅瀬を防衛するため部隊の一部は駐留し、残りは Wesmere へ向か"
"い、間違いなく森を守るであろうエルフ軍とで奴らを挟み撃ちにしようと。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:127
msgid ""
"While traveling there, I talked with general Morain regarding what had "
"happened during the expedition in the North, explaining what took place, how "
"I had ended up desperately commanding the evacuation and, in the end, the "
"rearguard delaying action.\n"
"\n"
"It was the first time I had talked about it all with someone who could "
"understand, who knew what it was like to lead soldiers, and who could "
"alleviate the ever-present fear that I had done something wrong, somewhere "
"along the way."
msgstr ""
"到着するまでの移動の際、僕は北方遠征の間に起きたことを Morain 将軍に話しまし"
"た。他にも、ここに来るに至った経緯や、いかにして軍の逃避を必死に指揮すること"
"になったか、そして最後に、後衛部隊による足止め戦略がどのようであったかも説明"
"しました。\n"
"\n"
"こんなことを話したのは僕には初めての経験でした。理解してくれて、兵を率いるこ"
"との何たるかを熟知していて、かつ、一人どこかで過ちを犯していないかという常に"
"付きまとう不安を和らげてくれる、そういう人に全てを話せたのです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:132
msgid ""
"We soon arrived on the edge of the forest, where the orcs were regrouping "
"their survivors with the forces attacking Wesmere.\n"
"\n"
"To prevent them from fleeing, Anówien had led her forces slightly to the "
"north, to cut off any escape route through the mountains."
msgstr ""
"森の端へはまもなく到着しました。そこではオークが、Wesmere に攻め込む軍勢を整"
"えるため、生存者を再集結させていました。\n"
"\n"
"奴らが逃亡しないよう、Anówien は予め自軍をやや北側へと移動させ、山間部を抜け"
"る逃げ道を遮断しようとしていました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:138
msgid ""
"The encirclement was in place, now all we needed to do was to finish this."
msgstr "包囲網は完璧です。さあ、あとは作戦を成功させることだけです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:141
msgid ""
"Chapter Thirty-Three\n"
"<i>Cornered And Slain</i>"
msgstr ""
"第33章\n"
"<i>窮鼠に迫る </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=AS
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:159
msgid ""
"So, the orcs have obtained some reinforcements, interesting... though these "
"do seem too exhausted to be such..."
msgstr ""
"さてさて、オークたちは援軍を得たのね、興味深いわ... それにしても、その援軍さ"
"んたちは、疲れ切ってるようにも見えるけれど..."

#. [message]: speaker=OL
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:163
msgid "What happened, warlord Bakor?"
msgstr "Bakor 将軍！ 何があったんですか？"

#. [message]: speaker=B1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:167
msgid ""
"The humans, assisted by some elves, have pushed us back! Prepare for an "
"attack!"
msgstr ""
"人間どもがエルフの手を借りて、俺たちを押し返して来やがった！攻撃準備だ！"

#. [message]: speaker=OL
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:171
msgid ""
"A shameful display... and to think that you were one of Great Chief Vrodar's "
"most trusted servants."
msgstr ""
"醜態を晒したもんだぜ... あんた、大族長 Vrodar が一番信頼する部下の一人だって"
"のによ。"

#. [message]: speaker=B1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:175
msgid "You utter fool, this is no time for—"
msgstr "何だと、この野郎、くだらねえ事を言ってる場合じゃ――"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:179
msgid "They ran quite far..."
msgstr "奴ら、随分と遠くに逃げていった..."

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:183
msgid "But now no more. Let us end them."
msgstr "ま、もうこれ以上はないだろうな、終わりにしようか。"

#. [message]: speaker=B1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:187
msgid "We must break through now or we will all die!"
msgstr "俺たちゃ突破しなきゃなんねえ、でなきゃ全員あの世行きだぞ！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:196
msgid ""
"This is taking too long, at this rate some of their reinforcements will be "
"able to mount an attack on the Ford before we finish this!"
msgstr ""
"このままでは時間が掛かり過ぎる。このペースだと、私たちが決着を付ける前に浅瀬"
"に奴らの援軍が攻撃を仕掛けて来かねない！"

#. [message]: speaker=B1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:209
msgid "No, this cannot be!"
msgstr "なんでだ、あり得ねえ！"

#. [message]: speaker=second_unit
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:213
msgid "That is what all those like you deserve!"
msgstr "お前たちみたいな奴には、それが一番ふさわしい！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:223
msgid ""
"With their leaders dead, the remaining troops should not be too much of a "
"problem to handle."
msgstr "奴らのリーダーが死んだから、後はそれほど手間の掛からない奴らのはずだ。"

#. [message]: speaker=AS
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:227
msgid ""
"Indeed, and I am thankful for your assistance. They have lost quite a few "
"soldiers, this will give us an advantage in the war."
msgstr ""
"ほんとに、皆さんの支援には感謝いたします。敵は相当数の兵士を失っていますか"
"ら、この戦いによって、有利になりますわね。"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:231
msgid ""
"Quite right, lady Nilmadia, and let us hope this victory will be the first "
"of many."
msgstr ""
"まったくその通りですわ、Nilmadia さん。さあ、この勝利が、今後勝ち取る多くの勝"
"利の始まりとなることを祈りましょう。"

#. [message]: speaker=AS
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:235
msgid ""
"Let us make it so, o Silent Princess... In any case, you should all come "
"with me, there are matters—"
msgstr ""
"そうしなければいけませんわね、静かなる王女様... とにかく、私にご同行なさって"
"ください。いろんなことが―"

#. [message]: type=Elvish Lord
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:257
msgid "(<i>Whispers something to Nilmadia </i>)"
msgstr "(<i> Nilmadia に何か囁く </i>)"

#. [message]: speaker=AS
#: war_and_home/scenarios/33_Cornered_And_Slain.cfg:261
msgid ""
"It seems victories will follow indeed, human and elvish forces led by your "
"northern princess have relieved Elensefar and are sieging Glamdrol as we "
"speak. Come, let us head within the forest, that we may have a proper war "
"council."
msgstr ""
"どうやら、勝利は重なるものなのね、あなた方の、北の王女を連れた人間とエルフの"
"軍隊が Elensefarを解放したそうよ、しかも、Glamdrol を包囲しているって。さあ、"
"森へ向かいましょう、きちんと作戦会議を開かなければ。"

#. [scenario]: id=34_Battle_Of_Carcyn
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:6
msgid "Battle Of Carcyn"
msgstr "Carcyn の戦い"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:140
msgid ""
"There had indeed been movement on the other side of the front for, "
"unbeknownst to us, while Anówien and I had yet to reach the ford of Abez, "
"Caror and Lumiclya led the counterattack, facing the orcs in battle near "
"Carcyn."
msgstr ""
"僕らの知らぬ間に前線の反対側では既に動きがありました。Anówien と僕が Abez の"
"浅瀬に向かっていた頃、Caror と Lumicya は反撃の先頭に立って Carcyn 近辺でオー"
"クとの先頭を繰り広げていたのです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:144
msgid ""
"Chapter Thirty-Four\n"
"<i>The Battle Of Carcyn</i>"
msgstr ""
"第34章\n"
"<i>Carcyn の戦い </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=NB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:260
msgid "The army is ready for the battle, we should have more than enough men."
msgstr "兵たちは戦闘準備を整えた、頭数はもう十分揃ったぞ。"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:264
msgid ""
"Indeed, and we shall have additional troops from the Grey Woods, for though "
"they are sparsely populated, they are still a seat of the Ka'lian and its "
"garrison has sent us reinforcements."
msgstr ""
"ええ、それに Grey Wood からの兵力も加わりますわ。住民の数こそ少ないけれど、今"
"持って Ka'lian の所在地ですし、守備隊が援軍を送ってきています。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:268
msgid "Good, now that everything's in place, we can finally strike back!"
msgstr "よし、これで準備万端、整いました、反撃に出られますね！"

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:272
msgid "Yes, it is time to make them pay!"
msgstr "そうですね、今こそ彼らに代償を払わせる時なのです！"

#. [message]: speaker=OL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:276
msgid "The humans are attacking? Finally, perhaps we'll have a proper fight."
msgstr ""
"人間どもが攻め込んで来てるだと？ とうとう来たか、少しは「まともな戦い」ができ"
"るかもな。"

#. [message]: speaker=OL2
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:280
msgid "Good, more lambs to the slaughter!"
msgstr "いいねえ、仔羊どもをもっともっと屠ってやろうぜ！"

#. [message]: speaker=EN
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:284
msgid "For Lintanir, kill these wretched orcs!"
msgstr "Lintanir のために、この忌々しいオークどもを殺すのだ！"

#. [message]: id=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:299
msgid "We'll get bogged down fighting their reinforcements at this rate!"
msgstr "このままの調子では、我々は奴らの援軍との死闘で動きが取れなくなる！"

#. [message]: speaker=OL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:311
msgid "That was... a proper fight..."
msgstr "こんなもんだな... 「まともな戦い」ってやつは..."

#. [message]: speaker=OL2
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:321
msgid "How... they were too strong..."
msgstr "なんだよ... こいつら強えな..."

#. [message]: speaker=second_unit
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:333
msgid "For Lintanir!"
msgstr "Lintanir よ、永遠に！"

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:342
msgid ""
"They are routed, let us take care of the stragglers and then onward, to "
"Elensefar!"
msgstr "撃退したわね、さあ、残党を始末して前進よ、Elensefar へ！"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/34_Battle_Of_Carcyn.cfg:346
msgid "Yes, and after that... we will take the fight to them."
msgstr "ええ、それが済んだら... あの者たちに戦いを挑むわけですね。"

#. [side]: id=HL1, type=Master at Arms
#. [scenario]: id=35_Elensefar
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:128
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:6
msgid "Elensefar"
msgstr "Elensefar"

#. [side]: id=HL1, type=Master at Arms
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:133
msgid "Lord Mayor"
msgstr "市長"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:229
msgid ""
"Their morale heightened by this victory, the army headed immediately towards "
"Elensefar to relieve its people and its defenders from the siege they "
"faced.\n"
"\n"
"The city had resisted the orcish onslaught because of the strength of its "
"men and its fleet's naval supremacy which allowed it to receive both "
"supplies and reinforcements from Aldril and Blackwater Port."
msgstr ""
"この勝利は全体の士気を高揚させ、敵の包囲に直面している Elensefar の民衆を解放"
"するため、ただちに前進を始めました。\n"
"\n"
"この都市は、自前の兵力に加えて強固な海軍力により、オークの猛攻を跳ね除けてき"
"ました。海軍の優位性は、Adril と Blackwater 港の双方から、物資の供給も援軍も"
"受けられることでした。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:235
msgid ""
"Though it had managed to hold on, the orcish forces were growing more "
"numerous by the day and had reached the numbers necessary to launch a final "
"assault.\n"
"\n"
"The city would need far more help to hold off these orcs and, happily "
"enough, said help was arriving."
msgstr ""
"都市は持ちこたえてはいたものの、オークの軍勢は日を追うごとに増すばかりで、最"
"終戦を迎えられるほどまでに達していました。\n"
"\n"
"その軍勢に対抗するには相当数の支援が必要でしたが、幸いにも、その援軍が到着し"
"つつあったのです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:241
msgid ""
"Chapter Thirty-Five\n"
"<i>Elensefar</i>"
msgstr ""
"第35章\n"
"<i>Elensefar </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=HL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:262
msgid "Hold... the line... keep... fighting!"
msgstr "持ちこたえろ... 戦線で...　戦い... 続けるんだ！"

#. [message]: speaker=EN
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:266
msgid "The city will not hold without its commander!"
msgstr "指揮官がいなくなったら、この都市を維持することなどできませぬ！"

#. [label]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:279
msgid "Armoury"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=HL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:296
msgid "Push the orcs back!"
msgstr "オーク軍を押し戻せ！"

#. [message]: speaker=OL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:300
msgid "Storm the walls and take the city!"
msgstr "城壁を破壊しろ！ 町を奪うんだ！"

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:304
msgid "The city still holds, forward!"
msgstr "この都市は、まだ大丈夫よ、行けー！"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:308
msgid ""
"The tragedy that befell my home shall not be repeated, these orcs <i>will</"
"i> die."
msgstr ""
"あの悲劇、私の故郷に降り掛かった悲劇は二度と繰り返させません、あのオークたち"
"は<I>死ぬことでしょう </I>。"

#. [message]: speaker=HL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:312
msgid "Oh thank the lords, reinforcements!"
msgstr "天に感謝する、援軍が来たぞ！"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:316
msgid "We are here to help, Elensefar shall not fall today!"
msgstr "支援にまりました、本日、Elensefar が陥落することなどありません！"

#. [message]: speaker=OL2
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:320
msgid "Take the city and kill them all!"
msgstr "町を奪え、全員殺せ！"

#. [label]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:348
msgid "Pier"
msgstr "桟橋"

#. [label]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:353
msgid "Docks"
msgstr "船着場"

#. [message]: speaker=HL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:357
msgid "Our ships can ferry some of your men to the city if you can spare them."
msgstr "兵士を補充したいときは、数名前後を我らの船で都市に運び込めるだろう。"

#. [message]: speaker=EN
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:361
msgid "This could be helpful in pushing out from the city's walls."
msgstr "この城壁から奴らを押し出すには、役立つこととなりましょう。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:365
msgid "The question is, do we have the soldiers to spare?"
msgstr "問題は、兵士の数に余裕があるかどうかでしょ？"

#. [message]: speaker=HL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:369
msgid "In any case, the option is there, should you wish to use it."
msgstr "まあ、手段はあるのだから、使いたければ使えばよいのだよ。"

#. [note]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:383
msgid ""
"A ferry links the pier and the docks (you can move units from sides 1 and 2 "
"between them)."
msgstr ""

#. [note]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:385
msgid ""
"A ferry links the pier and the docks (you can move units from side 1 between "
"them)."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:419
msgid ""
"We will not be able to win against more enemy troops, we need to withdraw!"
msgstr "これ以上、敵の勢力が増したら、私たちに勝ち目はないわ、撤退しなくては！"

#. [message]: speaker=NB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:428
#, fuzzy
msgid "They are beaten, the day is ours and Elensefar is saved!"
msgstr ""
"奴らを倒したぞ、今日、この日は我らのものであり、この都市は救われたのだ！"

#. [message]: speaker=HL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:432
msgid "Indeed, and you have the whole city's gratitude!"
msgstr "そうとも、この町全体が、全市民があなたがたに感謝している！"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:436
msgid "Now let us head northward, to Wesmere and even further."
msgstr "さあ、北方へと向かいましょう、Wesmere へ、そしてそのもっと先へ。"

#. [message]: speaker=$unit.id
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:483
msgid ""
"Their armoury has some enchanted mail that they are willing to part with."
msgstr ""

#. [option]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:485
msgid "I shall repay their generosity."
msgstr ""

#. [option]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/35_Elensefar.cfg:509
msgid "Others will make better use of it."
msgstr ""

#. [scenario]: id=36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:6
msgid "A Legend Of The Elves"
msgstr "エルフの伝説"

#. [side]: id=KL, type=Elvish High Lord
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:122
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:126
msgid "Kalenz"
msgstr "Kalenz"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:163
msgid ""
"With Elensefar relieved, the next stage of the offensive could now begin "
"with the combined forces pushing north to reach Wesmere's western border and "
"take care of any enemies there.\n"
"\n"
"However, there proved to be little for them to do."
msgstr ""
"Elensefar が解放されたことで、戦いの場は北へ移すことが可能になりました。連合"
"軍は北方に有る Wesmere の西の国境へ向かい、待ち受ける敵を始末することが目的で"
"す。\n"
"\n"
"ところが、やれることなど何もないことが分かったのです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:169
msgid ""
"Chapter Thirty-Six\n"
"<i>A Legend Of The Elves</i>"
msgstr ""
"第36章\n"
"<I>エルフの伝説 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:188
msgid ""
"We have little intelligence on the orc forces around here, so we should be "
"cautious."
msgstr "この近辺でのオーク軍については何も情報が無いのよ、用心してくださいね。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:192
msgid ""
"Understood, I'll prepare the military bands, they'll distract the enemy."
msgstr "なるほど、軍楽隊の準備をしよう。敵の注意を逸らしてやろう。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:196
msgid "You— !... (<i>chuckles</i>)"
msgstr "あらまあ！... （<i>..うふふ.. </I>）"

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:204
msgid ""
"(<i>Sounds of orc screams and war horns, as well as clashing of steel on "
"steel echo from up ahead.</i>)"
msgstr ""
"（<i>前方から、オークの叫び声や戦場ラッパの音が。更には、鋼鉄どうしがぶつかり"
"合う音が響く。</I>）"

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:208
msgid "Let us hurry forward, it seems a battle is taking place!"
msgstr "急いで歩を進めましょう、戦闘が起きてるようですわ！"

#. [message]: speaker=OL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:265
msgid "H—how, you're just a lone elf... How did you—"
msgstr "くっそー、エルフがたった一匹なのに... どうやって―"

#. [message]: speaker=KL
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:269
msgid "I have some experience killing your kind..."
msgstr "お前たちのような者を殺した経験が何度かあるのさ..."

#. [message]: speaker=KL
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:304
msgid ""
"And who might you be? An army from Wesnoth and — oh! — some from Lintanir."
msgstr ""
"君らは誰だ？ Wesnoth から来た軍隊と― おや！ Lintanir 出身の者もいるのか。"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:308
msgid ""
"(<i>She, like the other elves, bows</i>) High lord Kalenz, it is an honor to "
"meet you."
msgstr ""
"(<I>他のエルフたちと同様にお辞儀をして </i>) Kalentz 閣下、お会いできて光栄で"
"す。"

#. [message]: speaker=KL
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:312
msgid ""
"I am sorry for the suffering Lintanir endured, had I known I would have "
"tried to help. I assume this army is meant to take care of the orcs this "
"side of Wesmere?"
msgstr ""
"Lintanir が苦難に耐えたことについて気の毒に思っているよ、知っていれば助力した"
"かったのだが。この軍隊で Wesmere 側にいるオークどもを始末しようというわけだ"
"ね？"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:316
msgid "It is indeed."
msgstr "お察しのとおりです。"

#. [message]: speaker=KL
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:320
msgid ""
"Then I would advise doing so and taking Glamdrol, as without it, the orcs "
"will not be able to launch a counterattack. I shall handle the few remaining "
"around here."
msgstr ""
"それなら、先ずは Glamdrol の地を確保することだよ。Glamdrol なしでは、オークは"
"反撃を開始できないだろうからね。この辺りに残っている奴らは私が始末しておく"
"よ。"

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:334
msgid "W—was that <i>the</i> Kalenz?"
msgstr "い、今の人物は <I>あの </I> Kalentz だったの？"

#. [message]: speaker=EN
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:338
msgid "Yes... yes that was..."
msgstr "ああ... そう、あれは、彼だった..."

#. [message]: speaker=NB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/36_A_Legend_Of_The_Elves.cfg:342
msgid "Oh..."
msgstr "おぉ..."

#. [scenario]: id=37_Flames_Over_Glamdrol
#: war_and_home/scenarios/37_Flames_Over_Glamdrol.cfg:6
msgid "Flames Over Glamdrol"
msgstr "Glamdrol を覆う炎"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/37_Flames_Over_Glamdrol.cfg:158
msgid ""
"Meeting a hero of elvenkind was something none of them had expected and, "
"though at first it left them speechless, it rapidly filled their hearts with "
"a newfound determination, for they now knew that true legends fought beside "
"them.\n"
"\n"
"Now, they headed onwards towards Glamdrol, the main orc city west of Wesmere "
"but still south of the Heart Mountains."
msgstr ""
"エルフの英雄と出会うとは、誰一人として考えていませんでした。最初は言葉を発す"
"ることすら忘れてしまいましたが、真の伝説が自分たちのそばで戦っていることを知"
"り、全員の心は急速に、新たな決意で満たされました。\n"
"\n"
"そして彼らは Wesmere の西でハート山脈の南に位置する、オークの主要都市 "
"Glamdrol へと向かって行きました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/37_Flames_Over_Glamdrol.cfg:164
msgid ""
"If it could be brought down, there would be no risk of attacks on this flank "
"and all forces could be concentrated towards defeating the orcish main "
"armies and retaking Lintanir.\n"
"\n"
"This would be the first battle fought on orc territory and many were anxious "
"to finally bring the fight to the enemy's land.\n"
"\n"
"And so, with everyone on edge, the assault on Glamdrol began."
msgstr ""
"もしこの軍を破れれば、側面から攻撃を受ける危険もなかったでしょうし、オークの"
"主力の軍隊を撃破して Lintanir 奪還に全軍を集中させることができたでしょう。\n"
"\n"
"オークの領土内での戦いは初めてのことでしたので、ようやく敵地で戦いに挑めるこ"
"とを多くの者が切望していました。\n"
"\n"
"こうして、誰もが緊張した面持ちで、Glamdrol への攻撃が始まりました。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/37_Flames_Over_Glamdrol.cfg:172
msgid ""
"Chapter Thirty-Seven\n"
"<i>Flames Over Glamdrol</i>"
msgstr ""
"第37章\n"
"<I>Glamdrol を覆う炎 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=B2
#: war_and_home/scenarios/37_Flames_Over_Glamdrol.cfg:191
msgid "Hold the line and protect Glamdrol at all cost!"
msgstr "戦線を維持せよ、全てを賭して Glamdrol を守るのだ！"

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/37_Flames_Over_Glamdrol.cfg:195
msgid ""
"Glamdrol is the last threat to our western flank, we must take it to win "
"this war!"
msgstr ""
"我が西方面において、Glamdrol は最後の脅威だ、この戦いに勝利し、獲得せねばなら"
"ない！"

#. [message]: speaker=EN
#: war_and_home/scenarios/37_Flames_Over_Glamdrol.cfg:199
msgid "Forward, storm their battlements, we shall take this city!"
msgstr "前進せよ、城の<b>狭間</b>を狙え、この都市を奪うのだ！"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/37_Flames_Over_Glamdrol.cfg:214
msgid "They have reinforcements! The siege will be broken, fall back!"
msgstr "彼らの援軍が来る！ 包囲網が破られるわ！撤退よ！"

#. [message]: speaker=B2
#: war_and_home/scenarios/37_Flames_Over_Glamdrol.cfg:226
msgid "Hold, for Great Chief Vroda—Aargh!"
msgstr "持ちこたえよ、偉大なる首領 Vroda...バンザ..あぅー！"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/37_Flames_Over_Glamdrol.cfg:233
msgid "Their commander is dead! They will not hold after this."
msgstr "敵の司令官は死んだわ！すぐに崩壊することでしょう。"

#. [message]: speaker=NB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/37_Flames_Over_Glamdrol.cfg:237
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Then let us finish here and head to Wesmere for we have a new campaign to "
"plan."
msgstr ""
"それでは、我々は Wesmere へ向かいましょう、新たな軍事計画が待っています。"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/37_Flames_Over_Glamdrol.cfg:241
msgid "Yes, we will be home soon..."
msgstr "ええ、もうすぐ家に帰れますわね..."

#. [scenario]: id=38_Reunion_In_Wesmere
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:6
msgid "Reunion In Wesmere"
msgstr "Wesmere での再会"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:85
msgid ""
"After the battle of Glamdrol, the human and elven forces headed back to "
"Wesmere to recuperate and plan their next steps, now that their western "
"flank was secure.\n"
"\n"
"Though these concerns occupied most of their thoughts, some welcome "
"surprises would soon help distract them instead."
msgstr ""
"Glamdrol での戦闘を終えて、人間とエルフの軍隊は Wesmere へと帰っていき、体力"
"回復と、次なる作戦を練りました。今や、西方の安全は確保されたのです。\n"
"\n"
"彼らの頭の中は、そうしたことでいっぱいだったのですが、ある歓迎すべき出来事に"
"よって、気分を晴らせたのです。"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:90
msgid ""
"Chapter Thirty-Eight\n"
"<i>Reunion In Wesmere</i>"
msgstr ""
"第38章\n"
"<i>Wesmere での再会 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:139
msgid "This palace is quite big. I'm happy you're here else I'd be lost."
msgstr ""
"この宮殿は、ほんとに大きいですね。あなたがここにいてくれて助かりましたよ、道"
"に迷っていたことでしょう。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:143
msgid ""
"(<i>Playfully</i>) I understand, there must be little room for brains "
"underneath that armour..."
msgstr ""
"（<i>おどけながら </i>） 分かりますわ、その鎧の下の狭い空間に、脳みそが入る余"
"裕なんて無いわよねぇ..."

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:152
msgid "Hey, that's mean... True, but mean... Oh hello lady Anówien!"
msgstr ""
"おい、何てことを... まあ、その通りだけど... おや、こんにちは Anówien 様！"

# speakder= ES ではなくて EA では？
#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:156
msgid "Ha, you are quite funny... (<i>She notices</i>) M—mother!"
msgstr "ははは、馬鹿なことを言って... （<i>気づいて... <i>）お、お母さま！"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:175
msgid ""
"Finally, you took quite some time before arriving... and here are the others "
"as well."
msgstr ""
"やっとお着きになった、到着するまでに随分と時間がかかりましたね... 他の方々も"
"ご一緒ですね。"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:217
msgid "Indeed, lady Anówien. We have arrived, finally."
msgstr "ええ、Anówien 様、やっと到着しましたわ。"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:221
msgid ""
"Good, there are a few people you should see before the war council. They "
"should be arriving soon... And here come the first!"
msgstr ""
"よかったわ、戦争評議会の前に会っておく人たちが何名かいるのです。そろそろ着く"
"はずですが... あ、一人目がやってきましたわ！"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:235
msgid "F—father! And Wolfie!"
msgstr "お、お父様！ それに Wolfie ！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:254
msgid "It has been some time has it not? I am really happy to see you too."
msgstr "久しぶりじゃないかな？ また皆に会えてほんとに嬉しいよ。"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:258
msgid ""
"(<i>Pointing at Caror</i>) He is the one, by the way... Although you could "
"have guessed as he is the only one without an elf at his side."
msgstr ""
"（<i>Caror を指さして </i>） ところで、あの男性がね... 多分、分かるとは思うけ"
"ど、そばにエルフが一人もいないのは彼だけだし。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:262
msgid "Uhh..."
msgstr "うーん..."

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:266
msgid "M—mother!"
msgstr "お、お母さま！"

# young = young ?
#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:270
msgid "I see. You did say he was an upstanding young man, right?"
msgstr "なるほどね。彼は頑強な若者だって、君が言ってたよな？"

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:274
msgid "I believe I did, yes."
msgstr "そうね、そう言ったと思うわ。"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:278
msgid "Mom!!"
msgstr "お母さん！！"

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:293
msgid "Then I am quite pleased to meet you, Caror. My name is Haldar."
msgstr "ああ、お会いできてとても光栄だよ、Caror 。私は Haldar だ。"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:302
msgid ""
"Uhhh... Likewise, Haldar. And I seem to see the rest of your people "
"following... Wait, is that—!"
msgstr ""
"うぅ... こちらこそ、Haldar さん。残りの人たちも一緒にいるようですね... え、あ"
"れは！"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/38_Reunion_In_Wesmere.cfg:317
msgid ""
"Hello everyone... I am quite happy to see you all again. How have you been?"
msgstr ""
"やあ、皆さん... またお会いできるなんて、とっても光栄ですよ。お元気でしたか？"

#. [scenario]: id=39_War_Council
#: war_and_home/scenarios/39_War_Council.cfg:6
msgid "War Council"
msgstr ""

#. [side]: id=EL1, type=Elvish Marshal
#: war_and_home/scenarios/39_War_Council.cfg:159
msgid "Ka'lian"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/39_War_Council.cfg:181
msgid ""
"This unexpected reunion overjoyed Caror, Merynian, Oweomyr, Lumiclya and "
"Isandir. We spent quite some time talking until the council began.\n"
"\n"
"This short amount of time was far from enough, however, and we resolved to "
"countinue our discussions afterwards."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/39_War_Council.cfg:186
msgid ""
"The Ka'lian was awe-inspiring, at least to us humans. Before us were some of "
"the oldest and wisest beings on the continent, adorned in regalia from "
"before mankind ever reached these shores.\n"
"\n"
"And now, we would begin planning the counter-offensive besides them."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/39_War_Council.cfg:191
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Chapter Thirty-Nine\n"
"<i>War Council</i>"
msgstr ""
"第35章\n"
"<i>Elensefar </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=EL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/39_War_Council.cfg:210
msgid ""
"We humbly welcome you amongst us, Princess Lumiclya. Know that we grieve the "
"loss of our kin as well and will spare no effort to see Lintanir retaken."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EL2
#: war_and_home/scenarios/39_War_Council.cfg:214
msgid ""
"It seems you have already assembled quite a force and some mighty allies."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/39_War_Council.cfg:219
msgid ""
"We thank you for your concern. Let us now all endavour to push the orcs back "
"as fast as possible."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=AS
#: war_and_home/scenarios/39_War_Council.cfg:223
msgid "We shall all strive to accomplish this. Now, let us begin to plan."
msgstr ""

#. [scenario]: id=40_Doors_Of_Knalga
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:7
msgid "Doors of Knalga"
msgstr ""

#. [side]: id=HL2, type=Ranger
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:148
msgid "Dwarven Doors"
msgstr ""

#. [side]: id=HL2, type=Ranger
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:153
msgid "Rhenyc"
msgstr ""

#. [side]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:184
msgid "Knalga"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:314
msgid ""
"The plans for the next steps of the war were finally settled. The joint army "
"from Wesnoth and Lintanir would head East and North to free the occupied "
"territories.\n"
"\n"
"It would begin by ascertaining the state of Knalga and render aid as needed. "
"Afterwards, it would start freeing the land from orcish subjugation, "
"beginning with Merlyc before heading North, to Lintanir forest."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:319
msgid ""
"Wesmere's armies would handle the western passes while Wesnoth's ones would "
"be kept in reserve, as well as assisting in the East. Thus, neither could "
"spare many soldiers for our forces and both Nilmadia as well as Sidry would "
"return to their previous posts. However, they would provide us with supplies "
"while some impetuous scions of their noble houses decided to help us more "
"directly by joining the army.\n"
"\n"
"With these plans we set forth, headed to Dwarven Doors and Knalga, to "
"provide aid and to start pushing back the orcs."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:324
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Chapter Fourty\n"
"<i>Doors of Knalga</i>"
msgstr ""
"第4章\n"
"<i>Lintanir への道 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=HL2
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:346
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hold the line! The dwarfs will be here soon!"
msgstr "頑張るんだ！数日すれば主力部隊が到着するからな！"

#. [message]: speaker=OL2
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:350
msgid "Your people will die and so will the dwarves!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EN
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:354
msgid ""
"The humans have been pushed back quite far and there are no signs of the "
"dwarves. This looks grim."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:358
msgid "They will not fall today. We <i>are</i> here, after all."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=OL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:362
msgid "Oh my, more fools to play with. I will handle them."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:366
msgid ""
"Because of the reinforcements from the Ka'lian, Lumiclya and Anówien can now "
"recruit elvish nobles."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:379
msgid ""
"They will have too much time to fortify their positions at Merlyc, it will "
"be a slaughter we cannot afford!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=NB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:391
msgid ""
"Finally, their leaders are dead. Now we need only kill the scattered "
"remnants."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=DL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:395
msgid ""
"I thank ye for yer help against the orcs. I assume, by your presence, that "
"both Wesmere and Wesnoth march to war."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:399
msgid ""
"You assume correctly. We march to push back the orcs as far away as "
"possible. Any assistance your people could render would be greatly "
"appreciated."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=DL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:403
msgid ""
"Aye. I shall inform my king of the events of today. Best of luck to you."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=HL2
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:415
msgid "Don't give them any groun—!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: id=OL1, OL2
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:419
msgid "He's dead, now seize what remains of their fortifications!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EN
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:423
msgid "It will take far too long to dislodge them from there!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=DL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:437
msgid "Hold, for Knalga, hol—"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: id=OL1, OL2
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:441
msgid "Push forward, crush the dwarves!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:445
msgid "No... This will be a slaughter..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:463
msgid "These orcs are quite strong. Progress is far too slow, I fear."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:467
msgid ""
"Perhaps, but what can we do? We do not have more troops we can magically "
"conjure from nothing."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:477
msgid ""
"Suddenly, great noises rang out in the valley, a chorus of war horns "
"bouncing off the mountainside..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:490
msgid "And with them, the towering gates of Knalga opened."
msgstr ""

#. [unit]: id=DL1, type=Dwarvish Lord
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:503
msgid "Nardring"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=DL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:511
msgid "Stand strong lads, let's get'em!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=DL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/40_Doors_Of_Knalga.cfg:524
#, fuzzy
msgid "Wait... what do you mean the orcs are already defeated?"
msgstr "それには時間がかかるな。オークどもが、もうここに来ている！"

#. [scenario]: id=41_Secure_Merlyc
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:7
msgid "Secure Merlyc"
msgstr ""

#. [note]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:30
msgid "The orcs will not leave their fortress."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:249
msgid ""
"With our rear flank secured as well as promises of help from the dwarves we "
"headed East towards Merlyc to free it from the grasp of the orcs and to use "
"it as a resupply point.\n"
"\n"
"What a twist of fate it was for us to return to this place, the site of so "
"many of our battles."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:254
msgid ""
"It was quite different from before, however, as the orcs had heavily "
"fortified it, erecting new walls and digging moats.\n"
"\n"
"We nonetheless had no choice but to assault it to advance and thus our army "
"readied itself for a pitched battle."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:259
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Chapter Fourty-One\n"
"<i>Secure Merlyc</i>"
msgstr ""
"第1章\n"
"<i>救出 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:277
msgid ""
"And so we return to Merlyc once more. After this I shall be quite happy to "
"never see it again."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:281
msgid ""
"But you know it so well, you'll probably be named garrison commander! And "
"it's so close to Lintanir! Isandir can visit all the time!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EN
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:285
msgid "(<i>Synchronized, their faces reddening</i>) S—shut up!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=NB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:289
msgid "That uh... that joke works on you as well, you do know that, right?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:293
msgid ""
"And on you too, though you'll probably be the one visiting others instead. "
"I'd bet Lumiclya will be busier than you."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:297
msgid "(<i>Both of them redden as well</i>) S—shut up!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:301
msgid ""
"(<i>To Anówien</i>) It seems he has developed some immunity to such attacks, "
"no doubt thanks to you."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:305
msgid "Undoubtedly, though our dear daughter has not yet done so."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:309
msgid ""
"(<i>Her face beet-red</i>) Mother!... Perhaps we should focus on the battle "
"ahead instead."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=HR
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:319
msgid ""
"They are too well entrenched. We will not be able to take this before their "
"reinforcements arrive or our supplies run out."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=B3
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:346
msgid "Fools... so be it, taste my hammer! For the Great Chief!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=B3
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:358
msgid "Urk... no, master... If only reinforcements... had come..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:365
msgid "Merlyc is ours. We will eliminate the stragglers and then resupply."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EN
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:369
msgid "And then onwards, to the North... and Lintanir..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=unit
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:384
#, fuzzy
msgid "The enemy's here!"
msgstr "ここにはイノシシが！"

#. [message]: speaker=second_unit
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:392
msgid "Those fortifications are enormous!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=B3
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:396
msgid "You won't pass this fortress! We'll stop you here for the Great Chief!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:400
msgid ""
"They kept themselves busy indeed. I doubt they will venture out of the "
"fortress to fight us."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:404
msgid "We will need to force our way in to take Merlyc back."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: id=OL1, OL2
#: war_and_home/scenarios/41_Secure_Merlyc.cfg:429
msgid ""
"They are overrunning us, where are the reinforcements? They were supposed to "
"be here a week ago!"
msgstr ""

#. [scenario]: id=43_Where_Monsters_Fought
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:7
msgid "Where Monsters Fought"
msgstr ""

#. [note]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:28
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:32
msgid ""
"Cost of movement on frozen terrain (snow, ice, etc.) is reduced to 2 "
"movement points (if it was 3 or more)."
msgstr ""

#. [side]: id=UL2, type=Revenant
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:202
#: war_and_home/utils/characters.cfg:99
msgid "Sidry"
msgstr "Sidry"

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:221
msgid ""
"The journey to Lintanir was surprisingly uneventful as we encountered almost "
"no orc patrols. This, combined with the lack of enemy reinforcements in the "
"previous battle, seemed to imply that the orc garrison had been destroyed or "
"at the very least cut off.\n"
"\n"
"While this gave hope to many elves that, somehow, their loved ones had "
"survived, many others could not help but have a sinking feeling that "
"something was deeply wrong."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:226
msgid ""
"This unease grew as we neared the city, for even though we began finding "
"many signs of battles, there never were bodies left behind. The forest also "
"seemed to grow ever more sickly as we approached, with more and more trees "
"naught but hollow trunks.\n"
"\n"
"However, while this made us quite concerned, it did not change our "
"destination."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:231
msgid ""
"And so, we stood before the gates of Lintanir much as we did before, wary of "
"whatever we might find within."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:234
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Chapter Fourty-Two\n"
"<i>Where Monsters Fought</i>"
msgstr ""
"第23章\n"
"<i>修道院 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=NB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:256
msgid "What happened here? The defenses have been rebuilt yet none man them?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:260
msgid "We should proceed cautiou— Oh lords!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=UL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:292
msgid "Kill... Kill..! Kill!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EN
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:312
#, fuzzy
msgid "No... This cannot be..."
msgstr "なんでだ、あり得ねえ！"

#. [message]: speaker=EA
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:316
msgid "What monster could have done this?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:364
msgid "To have raised so many... A great darkness is arrayed against us..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:368
msgid "Let us grant them peace... and death to the one who raised them..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MK
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:385
msgid "Fools! The orcs are here, you have only weakened us all!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:396
msgid ""
"No, we are still fighting the undead! We will be surrounded! Oh lords, "
"please help us!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MK
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:414
msgid ""
"You fools have ruined my control over these puppets! Fine then, face the "
"orcs yourselves! They are already marching to retake this place!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:451
msgid "He will not escape! Send out patrols to find him, I want his head!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=NB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:455
msgid ""
"Lumiclya, I am sorry but the orcs are undoubtedly coming, we must ready "
"ourselves for them."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:459
msgid "I— I know... damn it all, I know..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MK
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:506
msgid "What's all that racket?... Wait, who dares destroy my puppets!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EN
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:510
msgid ""
"The armies of Wesnoth and elvenkind, reclaiming Lintanir from your dark "
"claws!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MK
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:514
msgid "Fools, this was the best way to fight the orcs."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:518
#, fuzzy
msgid "You will die for this, foul monster!"
msgstr "これ以上、民衆を恐怖に陥れるべきではない！"

#. [message]: speaker=MK
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:522
msgid ""
"No, <i>you will</i>. (<i>To Turod</i>) And as for you, it seems you came "
"back to lead my armies after all."
msgstr ""

#. [objective]: condition=win
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:528
#, fuzzy
msgid "Defeat Mal Keshar"
msgstr "Mal Keshar"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:569
msgid "Eärindel left us his sword... a final gift."
msgstr ""

#. [option]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:571
#, fuzzy
msgid "I shall wield it... in his memory."
msgstr "私はこの燃え立つ怒りを、誇りを持って振るうであろう。"

#. [option]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:598
msgid "Isandir trained with him in his youth... He will make better use of it."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=unit
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:629
msgid "Rooargh—"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MK
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:639
msgid "No, my dragon! Foolish mortals, I will enjoy breaking you!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:643
msgid "Good, we brought it down. Onwards, to the lich next!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=UL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:658
#, fuzzy
msgid "Prin...cess..."
msgstr "残念です、王女様..."

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:662
msgid "Eärindel... I shall free you from this, I swear."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:675
msgid "You have served long past what duty demanded. Go now, and rest."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=UL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:679
msgid "Thank you... my Queen..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: race=elf, human
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:698
msgid "Eärindel... May you find peace."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=UL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:702
#, fuzzy
msgid "Death... Death...! Death!"
msgstr "うぐぐ.... 退却するしかねえ！"

#. [message]: race=human, elf
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:721
msgid "Go now, and finally rest."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=UL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:725
msgid "Thank you..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=UL1
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:738
msgid "Care... for her..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=NB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:742
msgid "Rest easy, for I shall do so."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: race=elf, human
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:763
msgid "General Sidry... We will free you from this wretched state."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=UL2
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:767
msgid "Hate... Hate...! Hate!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=UL2
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:780
msgid "Protect... the realm..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: race=human, elf
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:790
msgid "We will, rest assured."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MK
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:811
msgid ""
"I presume you were the one ruling over this ruin? Judging by the number of "
"elven corpses when I arrived, you seem to have failed at that."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:815
msgid "Silence, foul monster! I will kill you for what you have dared do!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MK
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:829
msgid ""
"You were meant to be the commander of these forces, it seems you have "
"decided to face your fate!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:833
msgid ""
"No, I defy it! Today we will grant peace to all these souls you desecrated!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MK
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:847
msgid ""
"You... you were the one who helped that fool! Without you he would have "
"fallen far faster! You will pay for this!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=WM
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:851
msgid "G—go back to the darkness, abomination! The light stands against you!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MK
#: war_and_home/scenarios/43_Where_Monsters_Fought.cfg:883
msgid "Come at me if you dare, I am in need of corpses for my forces!"
msgstr ""

#. [scenario]: id=44_The_Final_Battle
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:6
msgid "The Final Battle"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:262
msgid ""
"Once the taint of undeath had been thorougly cleansed, we spent what days we "
"had before the arrival of the orcish horde fortifying our positions, "
"repairing the city and organizing supplies.\n"
"\n"
"During this time, the dwarves of Knalga sent us as much supplies as they "
"could, greatly increasing our resources, something that was highly "
"appreciated.\n"
"\n"
"At the same time, gryphons from Elzear's valley could be seen surveilling "
"the roads north, scouting for the orcs' inevitable arrival, providing "
"valuable advance warning."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:269
msgid ""
"Finally, as the eve of the final battle came upon us, we at least felt "
"confident that we were as prepared as possible. We spent most of the evening "
"conversing together before wandering off into smaller groups.\n"
"\n"
"Soon after we all went to sleep as this would be a fight for which we would "
"need all of our strength."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:274
msgid ""
"Come the dawn, we all readied ourselves for a last struggle. Vrodar and his "
"orcish forces soon appeared before us, more numerous than during his "
"previous assaults, probably because he had intended on dealing with the lich "
"before us.\n"
"\n"
"Though these numbers meant the battle would be harder than expected, it also "
"meant that it would be the last one. One more fight to break the horde and "
"free ourselves from its threat."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:279
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Chapter Fourty-Three\n"
"<i>The Final Battle</i>"
msgstr ""
"第23章\n"
"<i>修道院 </i>"

#. [message]: speaker=BB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:297
msgid ""
"So, the elves and humans have defeated those accursed undead. Well then, it "
"is their turn to fall, as they did here once already."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:301
msgid ""
"No, in the name of those whom you killed, we shall put you down. This, I "
"swear!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EN
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:305
msgid "The orcs shall pay for the death of our people."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=BB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:309
msgid "Meaningless bravado. You are surrounded, only death awaits you."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=NG
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:313
msgid "Much like it awaited your underlings?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=NB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:317
msgid "You are alone, and you will die just like they did!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=BB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:321
msgid ""
"Pah, enough of this foolishness! Forward, grunts! Gold and glory to those "
"who bring me an enemy leader's head!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:325
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hold the line, soldiers, and the day will be ours!"
msgstr "前進だ！奴らを皆殺しにして、領土をぶん取れ！"

#. [message]: speaker=CF
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:329
msgid "Fight well, for Wesnoth and for Lintanir!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=ES
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:339
#, fuzzy
msgid "This is taking too long, our supplies will run out!"
msgstr "時間がかかりすぎちまう、ボスに伝えてくれ!"

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:348
msgid "All their chieftains are dead, we have won the day!"
msgstr "すべての首領は死んだ。我々は勝った!"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:352
msgid "Indeed, and I do not believe they will return... Finally, this is over."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=BB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:383
msgid ""
"You're nothing but a cowardly princess who fled her city's fall only to "
"return to die there!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:387
msgid "Your head will roll for all those whom you killed!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=BB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:400
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:434
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:483
#, fuzzy
msgid "No! This cannot be! Nooooo—!"
msgstr "なんでだ、あり得ねえ！"

#. [message]: speaker=EP
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:404
msgid "Die, foul monster, and know all of your men will perish like you!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=BB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:417
msgid ""
"You're the one who held us back in the mountains! Seems like your death "
"didn't last... ah well, I'll ensure it does now!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:421
msgid "No, today it is your turn to fall!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=MC
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:438
msgid "Finally... Their horde should not recover from this."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=BB
#: war_and_home/scenarios/44_The_Final_Battle.cfg:470
msgid "Fools... so be it, face me and die!"
msgstr ""

#. [scenario]: id=45_Epilogue
#: war_and_home/scenarios/45_Epilogue.cfg:5
msgid "Epilogue"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/45_Epilogue.cfg:55
msgid ""
"With this victory and the death of Vrodar, the end of the horde had come, "
"now that it was both leaderless and armyless. The remnants of its forces "
"were pursued north, over the river Bork, beyond Dorest and Prestim, up to "
"the edge of the Silent Forest and the Desert of Death.\n"
"\n"
"The pursuit ended there, for supply lines were quite stretched and the "
"inhospitable lands before us would do the deed quite efficiently, leaving "
"naught but a few survivors to report to their Great Council in Barag Gór."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/45_Epilogue.cfg:60
msgid ""
"With the end of the orcish menace, rebuilding could now begin, and begin it "
"did. Lintanir in particular was a frenzied hub of activity under the "
"direction of Lumiclya. She, much like many of her kin, was determined to "
"return her home to its former glory.\n"
"\n"
"Together, they succeeded, and Lintanir became once more a source of awe "
"within the mind of others, ruled by a compassionate and prescient queen, one "
"who reminded many of her subjectes of valiant and courageous leaders from "
"times long gone, those whose tales were oft sung in festivites and names "
"bellowed as warcries, an honour she would surely soon receive."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/45_Epilogue.cfg:67
msgid ""
"Lumiclya would regularly send out patrols along the Listra and west of "
"Lintanir to keep the roads safe from bandits and to quell threats before "
"they grew to become a problem, notably keeping an eye out for the lich Mal "
"Keshar, who dared not show his face in the Northlands for a few centuries.\n"
"\n"
"She would receive help with the security of these lands from a familiar "
"source, for Oweomyr, after having inherited his family's titles, would be "
"mandated by the Crown to assist her. He would eagerly fulfill his mission, "
"as attested by how his vassals could often be heard grumbling he spent more "
"time up North than managing his estates."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/45_Epilogue.cfg:74
msgid ""
"They had little practical reasons for such complaints, however, as his "
"sister would masterfully take care of the house's holdings while he was "
"away, ensuring continued prosperity for all. She led developments in "
"multiple fields, both increasing their agricultural production by using more "
"of their arable lands, as well as enhancing trades with other nations, "
"whether the dwarves of Knalga or the elves of Lintanir."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/45_Epilogue.cfg:79
msgid ""
"She would obtain assistance with the latter from Isandir, dispatched to "
"nearby Weldyn as a special envoy from Queen Lumiclya to help coordinate with "
"Wesnoth's army and represent Lintanir's interests before its ally. He would "
"oft spend much time with Merynian between royal meetings, and they seemed "
"quite inseparable to the court."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/45_Epilogue.cfg:84
msgid ""
"After the war, Caror spent some time traveling the land, assisting others as "
"he could, though he would rapidly return to the army. After some time, "
"Oweomyr and Merynian offered him the fiefdom of Merlyc which they had "
"received for services rendered during the war, an offer he accepted.\n"
"\n"
"Under his guidance, Merlyc would be rebuilt into a vibrant trade hub as well "
"as a fortified base of operations for the royal army.\n"
"\n"
"All this new activity led to an economic prosperity its villagers had seldom "
"tasted before the war, and they were quite grateful for this new feeling."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/45_Epilogue.cfg:93
msgid ""
"Throughout all this, Sylindë was with him, whether on the road or in the "
"halls of their new home. She would assist the scouting operations in the "
"region, covering in a day what a normal patrol did in a week. She would use "
"these opportunies to watch over the wastelands to the east, often traveling "
"besides her father."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/45_Epilogue.cfg:98
msgid ""
"Haldar had indeed returned to his previous occupation of protecting the "
"villages east of the Listra. There, he spent his time traveling between "
"them, though he ventured further west than before, often stopping in Merlyc, "
"as always, Wolfie at his side."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/45_Epilogue.cfg:103
msgid ""
"He had managed to convince Anówien to head south with him, something she had "
"refused before, as she had felt that Lintanir was in need of all possible "
"druids. The war had however, somewhat unexpectedly, led to the rise of "
"multiple highly skilled druids which enabled her to delegate far more than "
"before. Now, when she was not visiting Merlyc or Lintanir, she spent her "
"time helping Elzear breathe new life into the wastelands."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/45_Epilogue.cfg:108
msgid ""
"Wolfie traveled with them for some time though as the years went by, he "
"seemed to spend more and more time in Merlyc with Sylindë and Caror, by the "
"fireplace."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/45_Epilogue.cfg:113
msgid ""
"Elaessa properly rejoined the church and rose in the ranks quite fast, her "
"dedication to others and her mastery of healing magic undeniable. She moved "
"quite a few times, and was finally named the high priestess of Soradoc."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/45_Epilogue.cfg:118
msgid ""
"As for me, I continued to serve in the army and was also moved throughout "
"the kingdom in command of various posts, before being enlisted as an advisor "
"to His Majesty Garard I, King of Wesnoth. However, at some point I was "
"offered command of Soradoc, and I took it, as Elaessa and I had grown "
"annoyed with the struggle to coordinate our postings.\n"
"\n"
"One day, I returned with Haldar and Elaessa to the shrine in the caves, the "
"one where she and I had fought the shadow and found the strange spirit. "
"Though nothing remained but the bare floor, the feeling of peace still "
"suffused this place, as though it would keep on offering a place for the "
"weary to rest and the hunted to hide."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/45_Epilogue.cfg:125
msgid ""
"At Haldar's advice, I plunged the sword I had been given here in the barren "
"stone floor. For a moment, nothing happened, the blade still and lifeless, "
"before glowing once more and emitting a great spark of light that bathed the "
"whole room in its warm embrace.\n"
"\n"
"Before us now stood the spirit, shimmering with light, yet somewhat veiled, "
"as though he truly was naught but an echo of something long gone.\n"
"\n"
"<i>I thank you for this gesture, and hope that, should it ever be needed, "
"another may find this sword and wield it in turn.</i>\n"
"\n"
"And with these words, the spirit disappeard, returning to wherever its "
"resting place was. We proceeded to leave as well, unsure of what we had "
"seen, though confident that we had done the right thing."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: war_and_home/scenarios/45_Epilogue.cfg:136
msgid ""
"In the end, though we faced a war and hardships that we did not expect, we "
"proved able to overcome these trials and in the end, found our own happiness "
"in these lands."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Adventuring Noble, gender=female, race=human
#: war_and_home/units/Adventuring_Noble.cfg:7
msgid "Adventuring Noble"
msgstr "冒険好きな貴族"

#. [unit_type]: id=Adventuring Noble, gender=female, race=human
#: war_and_home/units/Adventuring_Noble.cfg:14
msgid ""
"After some time spent on the road, away from their gilded halls, those "
"rebellious nobles who still live have gained some measure of experience. "
"They have traded their ostentatious dueling swords for plain ones and "
"refined their magical abilities, more than aware of the differences between "
"their old homes and the vast world and the need to be ready for it."
msgstr ""
"旅に出てしばらく経ち、華美な大広間から離れて、反抗的な貴族たちも、幾分かの経"
"験を積んできていました。それまでの派手な決闘用の剣から普通の剣へと持ち替え、"
"魔術に磨きをかけ、故郷と広大な世界の違いや、そのことへの備えの必要性をより深"
"く認識していました。"

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: war_and_home/units/Adventuring_Noble.cfg:24
#: war_and_home/units/Rebellious_Noble.cfg:24
msgid "dueling sword"
msgstr "決闘の剣"

#. [attack]: type=fire
#: war_and_home/units/Adventuring_Noble.cfg:34
#: war_and_home/units/Rebellious_Noble.cfg:34
#: war_and_home/units/Renowned_Noble.cfg:40
msgid "fireball"
msgstr "ファイアボール"

#. [unit_type]: id=Autumn Shyde, race=elf, gender=female
#: war_and_home/units/Autumn_Shyde.cfg:8
msgid "Autumn Shyde"
msgstr "Autumn Shyde"

#. [unit_type]: id=Autumn Shyde, race=elf, gender=female
#: war_and_home/units/Autumn_Shyde.cfg:24
msgid ""
"Though most of those who become elven shydes have achieved a bond with "
"nature in all its forms, some instead find themselves more attracted to its "
"cyclical side and reach an intimate understanding of a specific aspect that "
"calls to their hearts. From amongst those ranks come the autumn shydes, who "
"feel most kinship with that season. They are often prudent and wise, as "
"befits those who understand the most that winter and with it harder times "
"may soon come, and their counsel is rightly valued for such insights, though "
"one should not forget they are also powerful warriors who wield whirlwinds "
"of sharp leaves with which they bring down their foes through a torrent of "
"cuts."
msgstr ""
"エルフのシェード（Elvish Shyde）になる者の多くは形状の全てにおいて自然との一"
"体化を達成していますが、ある者はそれとは異なり、自身が持っている自然の循環的"
"な側面に魅力を感じ、心に響く特定の面に深い理解を示すようになります。そうした"
"者たちの一つが、秋のシェード（Autumn Shyde）で、秋という季節に最も親しみを感"
"じている者たちです。彼女たちはしばしば思慮深く賢明で、来たるべき冬とその厳し"
"い時期を最もよく理解している者としてふさわしく、またその助言は、その洞察力も"
"相まって正しく評価されています。但し、彼女たちが木々の葉による鋭い旋風と、切"
"り裂く激流を起こして敵を倒す強力な戦士でもあることは忘れてはいけません。"

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: war_and_home/units/Autumn_Shyde.cfg:48
msgid "falling leaves"
msgstr "落ち葉散らし"

#. [unit_type]: id=Brash Noble
#: war_and_home/units/Brash_Noble.cfg:7
msgid "Brash Noble"
msgstr "生意気貴族"

#. [unit_type]: id=Elvish Princess, race=elf, gender=female
#: war_and_home/units/Elvish_Princess.cfg:8
msgid "female^Elvish High Lady"
msgstr "エルフ大貴婦人"

#. [unit_type]: id=Elvish Princess, race=elf, gender=female
#: war_and_home/units/Elvish_Princess.cfg:21
msgid ""
"It is a misconception shared by many that the ladies of the Elves do not "
"participate in matters of war. Though they are generally less inclined to do "
"so than their male peers, they are powerful combatants nonetheless, and "
"their wrath is a terrible sight indeed.\n"
"\n"
"Some amongst their numbers take to it particularly well, developing rapidly "
"their magical abilities, notably their burgeoning faerie magic, and start to "
"feel as though they are discovering something within themselves that they "
"never knew they had, a flickering ember of power within that recalls some of "
"the legends of their people and one of the reasons why they are oft mistaken "
"for the fair folk."
msgstr ""
"エルフの女性は戦争に参加しないという話は、多くの人が抱く誤解です。男性ほど参"
"加に積極的ではありませんが、しかし、彼女たちは強力な戦闘力を持ち、その怒りの"
"気持ちは実に恐ろしいものです。\n"
"\n"
"その中でも、特に妖精の魔術に目覚めた者たちは、急速にその能力を伸ばして、それ"
"まで自分の知らなかった何かを発見したかのように感じ始めています。それは、民族"
"の伝説のいくつかと、彼女たちが時折り妖精の民と間違われる、その理由の一つを思"
"い起こさせるような、内なる力の揺らめく”おき火”なのです。"

#. [unit_type]: id=Elvish Queen, race=elf, gender=female
#: war_and_home/units/Elvish_Queen.cfg:8
msgid "female^Elvish Sovereign"
msgstr "エルフの元首"

#. [unit_type]: id=Elvish Queen, race=elf, gender=female
#: war_and_home/units/Elvish_Queen.cfg:22
msgid ""
"Some Elvish rulers, through the experience and pain brought by war, awaken "
"some spark of power hidden away within themselves. This small light, once "
"freed, is but the latest proof of what they have become. A lodestar to their "
"people, able to lead them through hardships with but a word and capable of "
"bringing to bear an echo of the old times, when the world was young and the "
"strength of the Elves had not yet begun to fade, from before the Great War "
"and the sacrifice of the Lost Light.\n"
"\n"
"Only the truly foolish or desperate face such a being in battle, for the "
"likes of its wrath have not been seen since before the arrival of Men and "
"Orcs from the Green Isle and the last sighting of such a force predates "
"perhaps even the emergence of the Dwarves from their tunnels."
msgstr ""
"エルフ族の統治者の中には、戦争がもたらす経験や痛みを通して、自らの中に隠れて"
"いた力の輝きを呼び覚ます者がいます。その小さな光は、ひとたび解き放たれると、"
"彼が何者になったかを示す最新の証左となります。たった一言で民衆を苦難から救い"
"出すことができ、世界が未熟でエルフの力が衰えだしていなかった時代 — 大戦"
"(\"the Great War\")と失われた光(\"the Lost Light\")の犠牲となる前の古い時代 "
"— を彷彿とさせる、エルフの民の拠り所となる存在なのです。\n"
"\n"
"そのような存在と戦うのは、本当に愚かな者か絶望した者だけです。その、怒りにも"
"似た存在は、人間やオークが緑の島(”the Green Isle”)からやってくる以前には目撃"
"されていませんし、一番最後に現出したのは、おそらくドワーフがトンネルから出現"
"する以前の時代にまで遡ります。"

#. [unit_type]: id=Elvish Royal, gender=female, race=elf
#: war_and_home/units/Elvish_Royal.cfg:18
msgid "female^Elvish Lady"
msgstr "エルフの貴婦人"

#. [unit_type]: id=Elvish Royal, gender=female, race=elf
#: war_and_home/units/Elvish_Royal.cfg:23
msgid ""
"Usually strongly connected with the earthly aspect of Elven magic, noble "
"ladies of the elvish enclaves are associated with wisdom and preservation. "
"As those entrusted with maintaining many of the more venerated Elvish "
"traditions, they play a large role in safeguarding the tranquility and "
"natural wonder of their renowned forest sanctuaries. Unlike their "
"counterparts in the lords, many of whom gain great individual insight "
"through their use of arcane magic, most ladies spread their power throughout "
"the societal orders that they guide, often at some cost to their own "
"personal abilities. For this reason, they serve most often as diplomats and "
"peacekeepers, holding high authority during times of amity and taking a "
"lesser role in times of war."
msgstr ""
"飛び地に居住するエルフの貴婦人は、常日頃からエルフの魔法の大地の相と強く結び"
"ついていて、知恵と保護に関係しています。彼女たちは、多くのエルフに高く崇敬さ"
"れる伝統の維持を任されていて、名高い森にある聖域の、その静寂と自然の驚異を保"
"護する役目を果たしています。貴族たちの多くは神秘的な魔術を使うことでそれぞれ"
"の見識をより深めていくのですが、彼女たちはそれとは対照的で、彼女たちが導く社"
"会秩序の隅々にその力を広げていて、ときに個人の能力を犠牲にすることさえありま"
"す。そのため、外交官や平和維持者として献身することが多いので、友好的な時代に"
"こそ高い権威を維持しますが、戦争の時代にはさほど力を発揮できない役目にありま"
"す。"

#. [unit_type]: id=Gryphon Transport {TYPE}, race=gryphon
#: war_and_home/units/Gryphon_Transport.cfg:6
msgid "Gryphon Transport"
msgstr "グリフォン空輸便"

#. [unit_type]: id=Gryphon Transport {TYPE}, race=gryphon
#: war_and_home/units/Gryphon_Transport.cfg:18
msgid "You should not be seeing this... Please do tell me if you do..."
msgstr ""
"こんなの、きっと、あなたは見たことが無いに違いありません... そうでないときは"
"教えてください..."

#. [unit_type]: id=Mornchild, race=human, gender=female
#: war_and_home/units/Mornchild.cfg:7
msgid "female^Mornchild"
msgstr "モーンチャイルド"

#. [unit_type]: id=Mornchild, race=human, gender=female
#: war_and_home/units/Mornchild.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Too often, the world is a harsh place, where famine and war course through "
"the land. At times, some desperate mothers have no choice but to leave their "
"infant at the doors of temples, where priests find them at dawn, like "
"childrens of the morning. Many of these are raised in orphanages maintained "
"by the clergy, and they often join when they come of age, trying to help in "
"some way so that no other children need be left alone upon a doorstep.\n"
"\n"
"Though they are not yet full-fledged white magi, mornchilds can summon the "
"light, both to heal their friends and ward off their enemies."
msgstr ""
"しばしば世界は、飢饉や戦争が頻発する過酷な状況となります。時には、絶望した母"
"親が幼子を寺院の門前に預け、夜明けに司祭に拾い上げられることもあります。そう"
"した子供たちの多くは聖職者が管理する孤児院で育てられ、成人すると、他のこうし"
"た子供たちが戸口に取り残されたままとならないように、何らかの形で手助けをしよ"
"うと入信することも稀ではありません。\n"
"まだ一人前の白魔術師ではありませんが、モーンチャイルドは光を召喚し、友人を癒"
"したり、敵を追い払ったりすることができます。"

#. [unit_type]: id=Noble Knight
#: war_and_home/units/Noble_Knight.cfg:7
msgid "Noble Knight"
msgstr "高貴な騎士"

#. [unit_type]: id=Rebellious Noble, gender=female, race=human
#: war_and_home/units/Rebellious_Noble.cfg:7
msgid "Rebellious Noble"
msgstr "反抗的な貴族"

#. [unit_type]: id=Rebellious Noble, gender=female, race=human
#: war_and_home/units/Rebellious_Noble.cfg:14
msgid ""
"Some scions of Wesnoth nobility develop a rebellious streak and go out into "
"the world, wether it be joining the army or adventuring to their heart's "
"content. This path is often taken by women of the nobility, whether to "
"escape marriages of convenience or just the stifling atmosphere of highborn "
"castles. Though they have often been trained in swordplay and at times in "
"the basics of magic, they lack knowledge of both the wider world and real "
"combat."
msgstr ""
"Wesnoth の貴族の子孫には、反抗的な性格が大きく目覚め、世界へ羽ばたく者もいま"
"す。軍隊に入ったりとか、心のままに冒険するとか。それ女性でも同じです。安易な"
"結婚話から逃れたいとか、城内の息の詰まる貴族生活からとにかく逃れたい、などな"
"ど。そうした彼ら彼女らも、時には剣術や魔術の基礎の訓練を受けはしますが、実社"
"会の経験や実際の戦場での経験は無いに等しいのです。"

#. [unit_type]: id=Remnant, race=undead
#: war_and_home/units/Remnant.cfg:21
msgid ""
"The remains of a soul who dedicated itself to the light. It lingers in this "
"world, for though it is lost in the shadows of time, it still hopes for its "
"dream to come true and it fights to make it so."
msgstr ""
"光に身を捧げた魂たちの名残りです。この世に留まり、時の陰に彷徨いながらも、夢"
"の実現を願って、今なお戦っています。"

#. [attack]: type=arcane
#: war_and_home/units/Remnant.cfg:25
msgid "faltering hope"
msgstr "揺れる希望"

#. [attack]: type=arcane
#: war_and_home/units/Remnant.cfg:37
msgid "desperate light"
msgstr "絶望の光"

#. [unit_type]: id=Renowned Noble, gender=female, race=human
#: war_and_home/units/Renowned_Noble.cfg:7
msgid "Renowned Noble"
msgstr "著名な貴族"

#. [unit_type]: id=Renowned Noble, gender=female, race=human
#: war_and_home/units/Renowned_Noble.cfg:15
msgid ""
"Once they have spent years, if not decades, traveling the land, little "
"remain of the youthful and naive nobles who wished to see the wider world, "
"unaware of its dangers. They have become hardened warriors, well-versed in "
"sword and sorcery alike and are well-known amongst their peers, both within "
"the adventurers and the nobility."
msgstr ""
"数年か、もしくは数十年か時間をかけて旅を経験すると、広い世界を見たいと願って"
"いた、彼らの、若くて純粋で危険知らずだった頃の面影は殆ど無くなります。逞しい"
"戦士へと成長するのです。剣と魔術に精通して、冒険者や貴族の間で名を知られるよ"
"うになります。"

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: war_and_home/units/Renowned_Noble.cfg:27
msgid "magic sword"
msgstr "魔法の剣"

#. [unit_type]: id=Winter Shyde, race=elf, gender=female
#: war_and_home/units/Winter_Shyde.cfg:7
msgid "Winter Shyde"
msgstr "冬のシェード"

#. [unit_type]: id=Winter Shyde, race=elf, gender=female
#: war_and_home/units/Winter_Shyde.cfg:24
msgid ""
"While most shydes become living avatars of the forests they call home, "
"others take to heart a specific aspect of the lands they protect. In the "
"northern wealds specifically, some find themselves attracted to the cold of "
"the snow and ice of the glacial lands they live in. These beings embody the "
"very wrath of their harsh winters, hurling the essence of the blizzard upon "
"their enemies who are left frozen, chilled to the core.\n"
"\n"
"However, much like the cold they bring to bear, they should not be mistaken "
"for beings of pure destruction, for the bleakness they harbour can be turned "
"into a soothing balm or a stout shield should they find something they wish "
"to protect."
msgstr ""
"多くのシェードが故郷の森の化身へとなる一方で、彼女たちが保護する土地の、ある"
"一面に心を惹かれる者たちがいます。北の森林地帯では特に、居住する氷河の雪や氷"
"の冷たさに魅せられるのです。その厳冬の猛威を体現し、凍える敵たちへ吹雪の神髄"
"を投げつけて、芯まで凍らせるのです。でも、そうしてもたらされる寒さと同様に、"
"彼らをただ破壊を行うだけの生き物だと認識するのは誤りです。彼らが抱く殺伐さ"
"は、守るべきものを見つけた時、それらを癒やしの香料や強固な盾と変えることがで"
"きるのです。"

#. [special_note]
#: war_and_home/units/Winter_Shyde.cfg:29
msgid ""
"The sprite (unit image on the battlefield) used is from Iris Morelle "
"(Irydacea/shadowm)'s add-on After the Storm, specifically the Elvish Avatar "
"unit."
msgstr ""
"戦場のユニット画像は Iris Morelle( Irydaces/shadowm ) 氏のアドオン \"After "
"the Storm\" のもので、特に Elvish Avatar ユニットを使用しています。"

#. [attack]: type=cold
#: war_and_home/units/Winter_Shyde.cfg:69
msgid "frostheart"
msgstr "凍えた心"

#: war_and_home/utils/characters.cfg:8
msgid "Turod"
msgstr "Turod"

#: war_and_home/utils/characters.cfg:33
msgid "Caror"
msgstr "Caror"

